WEBVTT

1
00:00:32.256 --> 00:00:35.054
Welcome back to SPEN Sports...

2
00:00:35.226 --> 00:00:39.027
...for another episode of
Are They Still Cool? Surf Edition.

3
00:00:40.563 --> 00:00:43.465
Cody Maverick was set
to become the biggest surfer...

4
00:00:43.633 --> 00:00:46.932
...to come out of Pen Gu
since Big Z Topanga.

5
00:00:47.103 --> 00:00:52.303
He shocked and awed fans and critics
alike with his fresh, new-school moves.

6
00:00:52.476 --> 00:00:55.603
He scorched nine-time champion
and local bully...

7
00:00:55.779 --> 00:00:59.146
...Tank "The Shredder" Evans
and was perfectly positioned...

8
00:00:59.316 --> 00:01:02.980
...to win the tenth annual
Big Z Memorial Surf-Off..

9
00:01:03.321 --> 00:01:07.348
I'm doing great, man. I think
I earned a lot of respect out there.

10
00:01:07.558 --> 00:01:10.116
After I win today,
you're gonna see a lot more from me.

11
00:01:10.292 --> 00:01:13.456
I promise. I'm going to the Outer Banks
to surf with the Hang 5...

12
00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:15.188
...the best in the business.

13
00:01:15.365 --> 00:01:20.269
It's been my dream since I was a little kid
and it's finally about to come true.

14
00:01:20.438 --> 00:01:24.671
Victory, fame and fortune
were all but guaranteed for young Cody.

15
00:01:24.843 --> 00:01:28.708
Until at the last minute, he chose
to protect his friend Chicken Joe...

16
00:01:28.877 --> 00:01:33.315
...from sore loser Tank Evans,
and gave up any chance of the trophy.

17
00:01:33.483 --> 00:01:35.815
Chicken Joe took home
first place that day...

18
00:01:35.986 --> 00:01:39.615
...and has since gained great fame
in the world of professional surfing.

19
00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:42.724
Maverick, however,
has been all but forgotten.

20
00:01:42.892 --> 00:01:45.326
Let's see what he's been up to
in this episode of...

21
00:01:45.495 --> 00:01:48.829
...Are They Still Cool? Surf Edition.

22
00:02:21.197 --> 00:02:23.097
So, Cody, why don't you fill us in...

23
00:02:23.266 --> 00:02:25.233
...on what you've done
the last few years?

24
00:02:25.401 --> 00:02:27.665
First, I have a question for you.

25
00:02:27.836 --> 00:02:30.066
I, uh... Okay, go ahead.

26
00:02:30.239 --> 00:02:32.834
Have you or someone you care about
expressed the urge...

27
00:02:33.009 --> 00:02:34.306
...to ride waves like a pro?

28
00:02:34.477 --> 00:02:36.707
- To be the master of the ocean?
- Come again?

29
00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:40.008
Well, I can show you how it's done
at the Pen Gu Surf Academy.

30
00:02:40.181 --> 00:02:44.676
At PSA, we got all the newest,
sickest moves at the lowest prices.

31
00:02:44.853 --> 00:02:47.344
You want backflips? You got it.

32
00:02:47.523 --> 00:02:50.084
Tail rides? You got it.

33
00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:52.956
Tube slides? Wah-ha!
You bet you got it.

34
00:02:53.163 --> 00:02:55.892
Whoa, whoa, whoa, man.
We're trying to do a show here.

35
00:02:56.064 --> 00:02:58.123
You can't just plug your surf school.

36
00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:02.134
Hi, I'm Lani,
lifeguard and co-founder of PSA...

37
00:03:02.304 --> 00:03:05.637
...where we're all about having fun
and being safe.

38
00:03:05.808 --> 00:03:10.767
Mention this commercial and get
30 percent off your first lesson free!

39
00:03:10.945 --> 00:03:12.936
Free, free, free, free.

40
00:03:13.115 --> 00:03:15.049
Don't waste your money on those losers.

41
00:03:15.217 --> 00:03:16.206
Oh, what now?

42
00:03:16.385 --> 00:03:18.546
You should learn to surf
from a real master.

43
00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:21.189
- Right, gang?
- Yes, sensei.

44
00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:24.120
Hi. I'm nine-time champion
Tank Evans...

45
00:03:24.293 --> 00:03:26.988
...and I want you
to discover your surf success story...

46
00:03:27.195 --> 00:03:29.220
...at Tank's Online Surf institute.

47
00:03:29.397 --> 00:03:32.231
Just send me your
parents' credit card information.

48
00:03:32.401 --> 00:03:33.425
Cut it out, Tank.

49
00:03:33.602 --> 00:03:36.469
- We're trying to film a commercial here.
- No, we're not.

50
00:03:36.638 --> 00:03:39.699
How can you promise these squirts
you'll turn them into winners...

51
00:03:39.876 --> 00:03:43.436
...when you've never won anything
in your life? Look at all my trophies.

52
00:03:43.645 --> 00:03:46.112
Each more spectacular than the last.

53
00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:49.773
Tank, my arms are getting tired.

54
00:03:49.985 --> 00:03:52.647
Fight through the pain.
It's part of your training.

55
00:03:52.821 --> 00:03:54.413
Wanna learn how to shred for real?

56
00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:59.424
Sign up now at TOSI and receive
a free participation trophy with purchase.

57
00:03:59.594 --> 00:04:02.257
Absolutely free. With purchase.

58
00:04:02.431 --> 00:04:03.830
Tank, get out of here.

59
00:04:03.999 --> 00:04:06.865
I'll also teach you about teamwork...

60
00:04:07.034 --> 00:04:10.264
...and proper surf etiquette!

61
00:04:10.537 --> 00:04:12.300
- Okay, cut.
- Wait, stop.

62
00:04:12.472 --> 00:04:15.237
- I am so getting fired for this.
- Stop.

63
00:04:15.743 --> 00:04:16.971
- Come on.
- Ha, ha, ha.

64
00:04:17.144 --> 00:04:18.543
Whoa, hey, wait. Hold on.

65
00:04:18.713 --> 00:04:21.114
I wanna tell you about
my franchising opportunities.

66
00:04:21.283 --> 00:04:22.614
With purchase!

67
00:04:22.784 --> 00:04:24.553
Ugh!

68
00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:34.858
Cody?

69
00:04:35.696 --> 00:04:37.288
Cody?

70
00:04:37.465 --> 00:04:39.491
Wake up, bro.

71
00:04:39.668 --> 00:04:41.793
It's me.

72
00:04:42.202 --> 00:04:43.965
- Cock-a-doodle-dude!
- Ah!

73
00:04:44.338 --> 00:04:45.566
Chicken Joe.

74
00:04:46.007 --> 00:04:50.809
Or as my Spanish friends call me,
El Pollo Loco.

75
00:04:51.779 --> 00:04:54.577
What made you
come back to Pen Gu island?

76
00:04:54.782 --> 00:04:58.478
You know, I haven't seen my buddies
Cody and Lani in like two years.

77
00:04:58.652 --> 00:05:01.314
And I finally got some time off
from my world tour...

78
00:05:01.488 --> 00:05:04.322
...so I thought I'd stop by and hang out.

79
00:05:04.492 --> 00:05:06.050
Time off from your tour?

80
00:05:06.227 --> 00:05:09.527
Aren't you supposed to be
in Madagascar right now?

81
00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:15.028
Oh, man. I gotta text my manager.

82
00:05:18.939 --> 00:05:20.601
Oh, wait.

83
00:05:20.808 --> 00:05:23.368
This is just a regular clam.

84
00:05:24.845 --> 00:05:26.367
Oh, I missed you, bro.

85
00:05:26.545 --> 00:05:29.777
Look at you, man.
Bigtime pro surfer now.

86
00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:31.247
I dig that wetsuit.

87
00:05:31.451 --> 00:05:33.750
Yeah? Thanks.

88
00:05:33.921 --> 00:05:36.583
It's a little tight around
my nuggets and tenders.

89
00:05:38.893 --> 00:05:42.691
But, my sponsors
like me to wear it, so...

90
00:05:42.861 --> 00:05:44.726
Dude, you have sponsors?

91
00:05:44.931 --> 00:05:45.920
Totally.

92
00:05:46.099 --> 00:05:50.058
They like to give me tons of free stuff.
Boards, wetsuits, wax.

93
00:05:50.270 --> 00:05:52.865
It's kind of a sweet deal.

94
00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:54.974
Yeah, it sounds pretty rad.

95
00:05:55.209 --> 00:05:56.299
Oh, it is, bro.

96
00:05:56.475 --> 00:05:58.137
And I owe it all to you.

97
00:05:58.712 --> 00:06:01.646
If you hadn't saved my life
and let me win the Big Z Memorial...

98
00:06:01.847 --> 00:06:03.907
...I'd never be where I am today.

99
00:06:04.084 --> 00:06:07.884
Heck, you'd probably be the one
with all the sponsors and endorsements.

100
00:06:08.054 --> 00:06:11.318
Surfing on the tour,
being on TV, screaming fans...

101
00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:13.958
Yeah, yeah, yeah. I get it. I get it.

102
00:06:14.126 --> 00:06:17.096
I'm happy for you, Joe. You deserve it.

103
00:06:18.565 --> 00:06:21.966
Hey, Cody. I picked this up for you
while I was on tour.

104
00:06:22.135 --> 00:06:23.261
Oh, thanks, Joe.

105
00:06:23.436 --> 00:06:26.835
I know how much you like
these super buff penguins.

106
00:06:27.005 --> 00:06:29.099
Wow, the Hang 5.

107
00:06:29.274 --> 00:06:32.004
Those guys rule.
Did you surf with them or something?

108
00:06:32.177 --> 00:06:33.941
Nah. I just missed them.

109
00:06:34.414 --> 00:06:36.814
You know those guys,
always traveling the world...

110
00:06:36.983 --> 00:06:39.646
...looking for the next
mondo extreme challenge.

111
00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:41.649
Too crazy for me.

112
00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:43.117
- Chicken Joe?
- Chicken Joe!

113
00:06:43.288 --> 00:06:46.917
- Penguin Lani!
- It's so good to see you.

114
00:06:50.429 --> 00:06:52.330
Chicken Joe,
can you teach us your moves?

115
00:06:52.499 --> 00:06:53.966
You're the "awesome-est"!

116
00:06:54.134 --> 00:06:55.861
Yeah, we wanna learn from you.

117
00:06:56.034 --> 00:06:59.334
Can you give us
a celebrity guest surf lesson?

118
00:06:59.538 --> 00:07:02.666
Yeah, I'd be happy to.
Let's get started right now.

119
00:07:02.841 --> 00:07:06.005
Find me some tacos.

120
00:07:08.047 --> 00:07:09.845
The Hang 5.

121
00:07:25.198 --> 00:07:27.027
Excuse me. Hey, I'm trying to see.

122
00:07:27.198 --> 00:07:29.190
- Come on, buddy.
- Cody Maverick.

123
00:07:29.368 --> 00:07:33.667
I am not spending my whole
entire vacation chasing after you.

124
00:07:33.838 --> 00:07:38.367
Mom, it's the Hang 5.
I've gotta be in the front. Wow.

125
00:07:44.248 --> 00:07:46.717
Ladies and gentle penguins...

126
00:07:46.885 --> 00:07:49.820
...it's the moment
you've all been waiting for.

127
00:07:49.988 --> 00:07:55.324
Behold the most extreme team,
surfing the earth and living the dream.

128
00:07:55.494 --> 00:07:58.587
Coming to you live in overdrive.

129
00:07:58.763 --> 00:08:02.597
Put them together for the Hang 5.

130
00:08:03.367 --> 00:08:05.734
Yeah! Hang 5! Hang 5! Hang 5!

131
00:08:05.971 --> 00:08:09.873
He's the big kahuna,
the leader of the crew-a.

132
00:08:10.042 --> 00:08:12.271
The mammal with a plan...

133
00:08:12.477 --> 00:08:14.876
...Mr. McMahon.

134
00:08:15.078 --> 00:08:16.170
Yeah!

135
00:08:16.346 --> 00:08:20.841
The king of the big-wave riders,
only 50 footers or higher.

136
00:08:21.018 --> 00:08:24.386
To him they're just ripples,
because the H is tripled.

137
00:08:24.556 --> 00:08:26.021
Introducing...

138
00:08:26.189 --> 00:08:28.384
...Hunter.

139
00:08:28.793 --> 00:08:30.420
Look, it's Paige!

140
00:08:30.595 --> 00:08:33.723
She's the best
trick surfer on the world stage.

141
00:08:33.898 --> 00:08:36.299
Her skill and audacity
cannot be gauged.

142
00:08:36.502 --> 00:08:39.197
She's beautiful, fearless
and full of rage.

143
00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:41.462
Let's give it up
for the one and only...

144
00:08:41.638 --> 00:08:43.299
...Paige.

145
00:08:43.507 --> 00:08:45.873
He's the Hang 5's enforcer.

146
00:08:46.042 --> 00:08:49.979
Even sharks and orcas meet their maker
when they go up against...

147
00:08:50.148 --> 00:08:52.742
- ...the Undertaker.
- I'm Undertaker!

148
00:08:52.917 --> 00:08:57.717
He's hardcore times four.
He lives fast, surfs hard.

149
00:08:57.888 --> 00:09:01.619
No regrets.
Don't call him crazy, call him...

150
00:09:01.792 --> 00:09:04.454
...J.C.

151
00:09:05.763 --> 00:09:08.732
If you want some, come get some.

152
00:09:14.171 --> 00:09:16.105
Wow!

153
00:09:21.746 --> 00:09:24.078
Why the long face?

154
00:09:24.248 --> 00:09:27.147
No, I was just remembering
the time I met the Hang 5.

155
00:09:27.316 --> 00:09:31.481
I worshiped those guys. Seeing them surf
made me who I am today.

156
00:09:31.688 --> 00:09:35.317
I worked hard my whole life
so I could be just like them one day.

157
00:09:36.427 --> 00:09:39.419
And somehow it just...
It just never happened for me.

158
00:09:39.597 --> 00:09:41.324
I mean, I love teaching the kids...

159
00:09:41.497 --> 00:09:43.864
...but I didn't think
that's all I'd be doing now.

160
00:09:44.301 --> 00:09:46.291
I always thought
I was meant to be somebody.

161
00:09:46.468 --> 00:09:49.927
Doing big things, inspiring people.

162
00:09:51.608 --> 00:09:53.702
I guess I was wrong.

163
00:09:55.179 --> 00:09:58.840
Does this have something to do with
all that stuff Tank said on the beach?

164
00:09:59.081 --> 00:10:02.279
Cody, you can't let that guy
mess with your head.

165
00:10:02.452 --> 00:10:05.387
He might have all those trophies...

166
00:10:05.589 --> 00:10:07.318
...but he's still a loser.

167
00:10:08.892 --> 00:10:11.222
Yeah, Tank is pretty annoying.

168
00:10:11.392 --> 00:10:14.794
- But it's not just that.
- It's not that hard.

169
00:10:14.997 --> 00:10:18.798
The secret to good surfing
is you just gotta feel the groove.

170
00:10:20.170 --> 00:10:21.967
Chicken Joe?

171
00:10:22.138 --> 00:10:24.630
Oh, I get it.

172
00:10:24.809 --> 00:10:26.707
Well, don't get me wrong.
I love the guy.

173
00:10:26.876 --> 00:10:28.537
He deserves everything he's got.

174
00:10:28.711 --> 00:10:33.239
But I can't help but think, man,
that could have been me, you know?

175
00:10:33.415 --> 00:10:38.251
Famous, successful,
a winner that everyone respects.

176
00:10:38.488 --> 00:10:42.183
I mean, look at him.
He's even a better teacher than me.

177
00:10:42.658 --> 00:10:46.321
Guys, I have officially lost control
of the situation.

178
00:10:46.495 --> 00:10:48.327
Cody? Lani?

179
00:10:49.699 --> 00:10:51.496
Okay, maybe not a better teacher.

180
00:10:51.668 --> 00:10:52.929
We're coming, buddy.

181
00:10:55.171 --> 00:10:56.864
What can I say? Pen Gu's home.

182
00:10:57.205 --> 00:10:58.194
I love my life here.

183
00:10:58.740 --> 00:11:01.574
I'd like to travel
and see the world someday.

184
00:11:01.744 --> 00:11:05.271
But right now,
I got the surf school, my lifeguard job...

185
00:11:05.447 --> 00:11:07.507
...and big waves all year
to keep me busy.

186
00:11:07.684 --> 00:11:09.675
It doesn't get any better than that.

187
00:11:09.853 --> 00:11:14.152
Man, this teaching thing
is harder than I thought.

188
00:11:24.701 --> 00:11:28.032
You know what I dig most
about Pen Gu?

189
00:11:28.202 --> 00:11:29.692
What?

190
00:11:30.238 --> 00:11:33.208
Nothing ever happens here.

191
00:11:33.375 --> 00:11:36.708
Chicken and penguin!

192
00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:40.280
Never mind. Something is happening.

193
00:11:40.449 --> 00:11:44.441
Wait. I've seen that seagull
somewhere before.

194
00:11:44.686 --> 00:11:48.747
Prepare yourselves. It's the moment
you've all been waiting for.

195
00:11:48.923 --> 00:11:51.722
The Hang 5! They're here.

196
00:11:51.927 --> 00:11:52.985
The Hang 5?

197
00:11:53.228 --> 00:11:55.424
The most legendary surf crew
of all time?

198
00:11:55.598 --> 00:11:57.291
- Yes!
- Woo-hoo!

199
00:11:58.700 --> 00:12:00.599
- Oh, yeah.
- Oh, great.

200
00:12:00.767 --> 00:12:02.463
Way to ruin the surprise, kid.

201
00:12:02.637 --> 00:12:04.468
That was supposed to be my line.

202
00:12:05.573 --> 00:12:07.735
You can still say it.

203
00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:09.844
You know what? Forget it.

204
00:12:10.012 --> 00:12:12.945
There used to be respect
for showmanship in this business.

205
00:12:13.113 --> 00:12:16.413
Wait a minute.
I'm the resident Hang 5 expert here.

206
00:12:16.584 --> 00:12:19.952
If they were coming,
trust me, I'd know about it.

207
00:12:20.122 --> 00:12:21.783
Hey, Hang 5.

208
00:12:32.767 --> 00:12:33.961
What's up, little dudes?

209
00:12:36.037 --> 00:12:37.869
You... It's...

210
00:12:38.307 --> 00:12:39.331
Oh, my gosh. My gosh.

211
00:12:39.842 --> 00:12:43.971
We get crazed fans all the time.
But it's like I always say:

212
00:12:44.145 --> 00:12:47.204
A brave man builds his house
on an ocean of milk.

213
00:12:47.381 --> 00:12:49.474
That doesn't make a lick of sense.

214
00:12:49.649 --> 00:12:53.984
It doesn't have to. I'm the boss,
and I like milk and fish.

215
00:12:54.155 --> 00:12:56.816
Because I'm an otter,
and otters like fish.

216
00:12:56.990 --> 00:13:00.016
I just wish you could milk a fish.

217
00:13:03.297 --> 00:13:06.164
I don't really know
what to say about that.

218
00:13:06.868 --> 00:13:09.735
Hey, bro. You know where
we can get something to eat?

219
00:13:09.904 --> 00:13:11.563
Uh, yeah, yeah. Food, right.

220
00:13:11.771 --> 00:13:15.139
You guys eat food because you're
the Hang 5. What about squid on a stick?

221
00:13:15.342 --> 00:13:17.810
Squids? On sticks?

222
00:13:18.011 --> 00:13:20.276
I love impaled food.

223
00:13:20.481 --> 00:13:22.540
Oh, yeah, I'll try anything.

224
00:13:22.784 --> 00:13:25.412
Oh, yeah?
Well, I've tried everything, twice.

225
00:13:25.586 --> 00:13:30.521
Whatever gnarly stuff you can eat,
I can eat twice as much, twice as fast.

226
00:13:30.723 --> 00:13:34.387
Jeez, Hunter. Why do you always
have to be so competitive?

227
00:13:34.594 --> 00:13:37.722
You know what? You should come over
to my place for a backyard luau.

228
00:13:37.898 --> 00:13:40.424
Come on. Come on.
I won't take no for an answer.

229
00:13:40.601 --> 00:13:44.366
- So you should just come.
- Yeah, man. Bring it on. I'm starving.

230
00:13:44.571 --> 00:13:46.698
Tell me more about these squid sticks.

231
00:13:46.873 --> 00:13:48.272
Hey, look at me, Hang 5.

232
00:13:48.442 --> 00:13:50.843
Whoa, hold on there. Be careful.

233
00:13:51.045 --> 00:13:54.673
I know all your moves. Like this.
Unh!

234
00:13:54.848 --> 00:13:57.543
Help! Lani! Help! Help!

235
00:13:57.716 --> 00:13:59.206
Oh, no. Arnold!

236
00:13:59.452 --> 00:14:02.854
- Kid!
- Hang on, Arnold. I'm coming! Hyah!

237
00:14:08.729 --> 00:14:09.718
Hold on.

238
00:14:09.897 --> 00:14:11.590
Whoa! Who's that?

239
00:14:11.764 --> 00:14:14.632
Oh, that's just Arnold.
This happens all the time.

240
00:14:14.835 --> 00:14:16.597
Lani's on it.

241
00:14:17.036 --> 00:14:21.906
Arnold, you know what I said
about going into the ocean by yourself.

242
00:14:22.075 --> 00:14:25.203
I know.
Thanks for having my back out there.

243
00:14:25.378 --> 00:14:26.638
Oh, ha, ha, ha!

244
00:14:26.846 --> 00:14:29.041
Whoa! You all right, little dude?

245
00:14:29.215 --> 00:14:32.309
Yeah. I was just trying
to show you my mad skills.

246
00:14:32.485 --> 00:14:36.286
Heh, heh. You shouldn't try to imitate us.
We're trained professionals.

247
00:14:36.456 --> 00:14:38.787
Some of us with huge muscles.

248
00:14:40.894 --> 00:14:43.486
I'm not gonna say who.
That would be bragging.

249
00:14:45.464 --> 00:14:46.556
Nice moves.

250
00:14:46.732 --> 00:14:49.997
Oh, thanks. You must be the Hang 5.

251
00:14:50.169 --> 00:14:52.297
Guess that explains the whale.

252
00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:55.298
Oops! I forgot to lock it.

253
00:14:56.641 --> 00:14:58.075
Hey, Lani. Guess what.

254
00:14:58.244 --> 00:15:01.110
I'm throwing a luau
for the Hang 5 at my place.

255
00:15:01.279 --> 00:15:03.612
Oh, yes. Let's luau!

256
00:15:03.782 --> 00:15:06.685
- All right!
- Yeah!

257
00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:14.023
Yes. Come on, Hunter.

258
00:15:14.759 --> 00:15:16.125
Whoo!

259
00:15:16.996 --> 00:15:20.329
Hang 5 is the real deal.
They've done everything.

260
00:15:20.533 --> 00:15:23.161
Snowboard during an avalanche, check.

261
00:15:23.402 --> 00:15:25.962
Skydive into a tornado, check.

262
00:15:26.172 --> 00:15:28.332
Competitive speed knitting, check.

263
00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:31.634
Whatever it is they're about to do,
I wanna be a part of it.

264
00:15:31.843 --> 00:15:33.470
T ell us a story, J.C.

265
00:15:33.679 --> 00:15:35.169
T ell us a scary one.

266
00:15:35.347 --> 00:15:36.473
Yeah! Yeah!

267
00:15:36.916 --> 00:15:40.648
All right. This happened
while I was on tour last year.

268
00:15:40.820 --> 00:15:43.719
We were surfing the infamous
ghost beach of Levesque...

269
00:15:43.922 --> 00:15:46.914
...where they say
even the waves are haunted.

270
00:15:47.125 --> 00:15:48.717
Wh... Were you scared?

271
00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:52.954
Not at first. But it was quiet. Too quiet.

272
00:15:53.165 --> 00:15:55.065
- Then this ghost wave grabs my board!
- Ah!

273
00:15:55.834 --> 00:15:57.424
And then what happened?

274
00:15:57.634 --> 00:15:58.829
So there I am underwater...

275
00:15:59.003 --> 00:16:01.836
He was held down
by almost 5000 psi of pressure.

276
00:16:02.006 --> 00:16:04.999
I read about it in your interview
with Rolling Waves magazine.

277
00:16:05.177 --> 00:16:07.077
- Escargot-go?
- Uh...

278
00:16:07.246 --> 00:16:08.644
No, thanks.

279
00:16:08.813 --> 00:16:10.247
I woke up on the ocean floor...

280
00:16:10.449 --> 00:16:12.711
I've practiced
your breathing technique for years.

281
00:16:12.883 --> 00:16:14.942
I can hold my breath
for almost five minutes.

282
00:16:15.118 --> 00:16:16.643
I'm trying to tell my story, bro.

283
00:16:16.821 --> 00:16:19.449
Can I show you my variation
on your five flipper shuffle?

284
00:16:19.624 --> 00:16:22.093
Go check on the Undertaker.
He's always hungry.

285
00:16:22.261 --> 00:16:23.592
Yes, sir.

286
00:16:23.762 --> 00:16:27.355
All right.
So there I was, 200 feet underwater...

287
00:16:27.531 --> 00:16:29.022
...and I'm freaking out.

288
00:16:29.234 --> 00:16:33.033
Did you do a controlled emergency
ascent to protect your lungs?

289
00:16:33.203 --> 00:16:34.603
Uh, yeah.

290
00:16:34.973 --> 00:16:38.204
- How did you know about that?
- Cody taught us that at our surf school.

291
00:16:40.913 --> 00:16:42.503
That guy?

292
00:16:42.746 --> 00:16:43.838
Um...

293
00:16:44.348 --> 00:16:45.542
Interesting.

294
00:16:45.716 --> 00:16:49.847
If you kids think J.C.'s dumb old stories
are cool, watch me uproot this tree.

295
00:16:51.256 --> 00:16:52.588
Unh!

296
00:16:55.026 --> 00:16:57.788
Anyways, wanna hear
about the time I fought off a shark...

297
00:16:57.960 --> 00:16:59.588
...with nothing but my camo shorts?

298
00:16:59.763 --> 00:17:00.787
Yeah!

299
00:17:01.865 --> 00:17:04.390
Mr. Undertaker,
do you wanna try some of the...?

300
00:17:07.438 --> 00:17:09.372
- More.
- Coming right up.

301
00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:11.475
Hey, have you seen my friend Cod...

302
00:17:11.644 --> 00:17:14.941
Whoa, man, don't eat me.
I'm not the food.

303
00:17:15.112 --> 00:17:18.206
Can you at least
lay an egg or something?

304
00:17:20.617 --> 00:17:24.110
Scary? Yeah, I get that sometimes.

305
00:17:24.289 --> 00:17:27.051
They say it's because
I don't smile or talk a lot.

306
00:17:27.223 --> 00:17:30.125
- But I'm just shy. Okay?
- Ah!

307
00:17:30.427 --> 00:17:31.894
Oh...

308
00:17:33.964 --> 00:17:35.956
Little of this, little of that.

309
00:17:36.134 --> 00:17:38.158
All right, add some spice.

310
00:17:38.335 --> 00:17:41.828
Oh, yeah. Prepping that squid.

311
00:17:44.907 --> 00:17:46.238
Would you like coconut water?

312
00:17:46.409 --> 00:17:50.471
- That depends. I prefer fish milk.
- Uh...

313
00:17:50.647 --> 00:17:53.081
All right,
then I'll drink your coconut water.

314
00:17:53.251 --> 00:17:58.277
But you better believe I'm gonna pretend
I'm sucking it from a fish's udder.

315
00:17:58.454 --> 00:18:01.321
You know, Mr. McMahon,
I do a little surfing myself.

316
00:18:01.490 --> 00:18:03.253
Cool, cool.

317
00:18:03.426 --> 00:18:04.859
It is cool. And you know what?

318
00:18:05.061 --> 00:18:08.190
I got some ideas for some tricks
that could really change things up.

319
00:18:08.365 --> 00:18:10.458
I'm talking next-level stuff, man.

320
00:18:10.634 --> 00:18:12.533
Oh, yeah? You'll have to
show me sometime.

321
00:18:12.702 --> 00:18:14.761
Really? Let's set a time.
How about tomorrow?

322
00:18:14.937 --> 00:18:18.430
Excuse me a second.
Can I have everyone's attention, please?

323
00:18:22.612 --> 00:18:24.773
What I hold here
is the key that will unlock...

324
00:18:24.948 --> 00:18:28.609
...one of the greatest mysteries
of our time.

325
00:18:28.883 --> 00:18:31.785
Why everything seems to taste like me?

326
00:18:31.987 --> 00:18:32.976
No.

327
00:18:33.155 --> 00:18:37.115
This is a map to the most legendary
surfing spot on the planet.

328
00:18:38.695 --> 00:18:40.890
The Trenches.

329
00:18:42.665 --> 00:18:46.327
I thought that the Trenches were
just, like, made up to scare little kids.

330
00:18:46.501 --> 00:18:51.735
Oh, it's real, all right.
And everything you hear about it is true.

331
00:18:51.974 --> 00:18:54.637
It's hidden somewhere
on Slaughter island...

332
00:18:54.811 --> 00:18:58.677
...the most dangerous
and mysterious place on the planet.

333
00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:01.315
Jagged rocks, huge cliffs.

334
00:19:01.517 --> 00:19:03.678
It's a surfer's graveyard.

335
00:19:03.886 --> 00:19:06.481
And we're going to ride it! RTL!

336
00:19:06.656 --> 00:19:07.645
Am I right, guys?

337
00:19:07.858 --> 00:19:09.552
Heck yeah. RTL!

338
00:19:09.759 --> 00:19:11.351
RTL!

339
00:19:11.694 --> 00:19:14.753
Hey, Joe. What does RTL mean?

340
00:19:16.698 --> 00:19:19.099
I don't know, man. Rumbly tummy...

341
00:19:21.036 --> 00:19:22.697
...something.

342
00:19:24.274 --> 00:19:27.833
Oh, I shouldn't have eaten
all those escargot-gos.

343
00:19:28.042 --> 00:19:31.034
Surfing the Trenches
will be the greatest ride of my life.

344
00:19:31.513 --> 00:19:33.208
And my last.

345
00:19:33.415 --> 00:19:34.882
Because you're gonna die?

346
00:19:35.083 --> 00:19:39.418
- No. Because I'm retiring.
- What?

347
00:19:41.090 --> 00:19:42.886
Boss, you can't be serious.

348
00:19:43.124 --> 00:19:46.787
Hey, I'm not getting any younger.
It's time for me to settle down.

349
00:19:46.961 --> 00:19:50.090
What does that mean? We're
gonna be the Hang 4 from now on?

350
00:19:50.266 --> 00:19:54.463
Maybe not. Big Z always said
Pen Gu breeds great surfers.

351
00:19:54.637 --> 00:19:56.434
I think it's time we add a new member.

352
00:19:56.605 --> 00:19:58.662
Have somebody in mind, boss?

353
00:19:58.839 --> 00:20:02.936
Ha, ha. I'm not gonna give away
the surprise just yet.

354
00:20:03.111 --> 00:20:06.980
But I think I might have found
someone very special.

355
00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:10.341
Yes!

356
00:20:12.486 --> 00:20:14.512
How totally awesome is this, bro?

357
00:20:14.756 --> 00:20:16.086
I'm gonna join the Hang 5.

358
00:20:16.256 --> 00:20:18.782
Can you even imagine
what that would be like?

359
00:20:18.960 --> 00:20:21.656
Yeah, that sounds pretty rad.

360
00:20:21.830 --> 00:20:26.598
But, um, are you sure Mr. McMahon
was talking about you, bro?

361
00:20:26.936 --> 00:20:30.370
What? Who else could it be, man?
He looked right at me.

362
00:20:30.604 --> 00:20:32.937
Hey, Cody. You up?

363
00:20:33.107 --> 00:20:34.369
Yeah. Hey, what's up, Lani?

364
00:20:34.542 --> 00:20:37.478
Hey. So, uh, you got a second?

365
00:20:37.646 --> 00:20:39.010
I need to tell you something.

366
00:20:39.180 --> 00:20:41.341
Sure. I was talking about
how great it'd be...

367
00:20:41.516 --> 00:20:43.244
...if the Hang 5 asked me to join.

368
00:20:43.450 --> 00:20:48.183
Oh, um, okay.
You think they might ask you?

369
00:20:48.388 --> 00:20:51.517
Well, yeah. I mean, why not?
I've been following them my whole life.

370
00:20:51.759 --> 00:20:53.454
And I'm the best surfer on Pen Gu.

371
00:20:53.628 --> 00:20:55.186
Who else are they gonna ask?

372
00:20:55.364 --> 00:20:57.626
Hey, Lani. I told my mom...

373
00:20:57.798 --> 00:21:01.029
...that you told me
that you were going to join the Hang 5.

374
00:21:01.200 --> 00:21:04.295
And then she said
that I should get your autograph...

375
00:21:04.471 --> 00:21:07.201
...because she wants to sell it online.

376
00:21:07.375 --> 00:21:08.364
What?

377
00:21:08.543 --> 00:21:11.740
Whoa! That's awesome, Lani.

378
00:21:11.913 --> 00:21:17.043
Cody, your imaginary friends
are gonna be so disappointed.

379
00:21:18.552 --> 00:21:20.885
So I guess they asked you.

380
00:21:21.089 --> 00:21:25.218
Yeah. Mr. McMahon and Paige
came over to my place this morning.

381
00:21:25.425 --> 00:21:27.517
They said I showed moxie
saving Arnold...

382
00:21:27.693 --> 00:21:30.491
...and they could use somebody
with my lifeguard skills.

383
00:21:30.663 --> 00:21:33.599
They're waiting for me
on the South Shore.

384
00:21:33.800 --> 00:21:36.496
But I don't know, Cody.
This is your dream.

385
00:21:36.670 --> 00:21:39.731
No. No, no... No way.
You can't pass this up, Lani.

386
00:21:39.941 --> 00:21:42.669
It's the Hang 5, all right? You gotta go.

387
00:21:42.842 --> 00:21:45.676
- I'll figure something out. Don't worry.
- Wait, really?

388
00:21:45.879 --> 00:21:47.505
Will you be okay? I don't want to...

389
00:21:47.680 --> 00:21:50.377
Go tell them you're coming
before they change their minds.

390
00:21:50.551 --> 00:21:53.918
- I'll see you there.
- Okay, okay. Bye!

391
00:21:54.121 --> 00:21:58.079
Does that mean you're not leaving
Pen Gu and joining the Hang 5...

392
00:21:58.324 --> 00:22:03.058
...and fulfilling your ultimate destiny
of becoming a legendary surfer?

393
00:22:03.230 --> 00:22:04.822
No, I got an idea.

394
00:22:05.032 --> 00:22:07.899
Come on, you guys.
I'll explain on the way.

395
00:22:08.369 --> 00:22:12.530
Hang 5! Prepare for boarding.

396
00:22:12.737 --> 00:22:15.036
Don't be nervous.
You're gonna do great.

397
00:22:15.207 --> 00:22:17.232
- I have a good feeling about you.
- Ha-ha.

398
00:22:17.476 --> 00:22:19.535
- Thanks.
- Is that them?

399
00:22:19.712 --> 00:22:21.112
Yeah, come on. Get over there.

400
00:22:21.281 --> 00:22:22.839
- Uh!
- Ah!

401
00:22:23.116 --> 00:22:25.880
Do what Cody taught us.

402
00:22:26.053 --> 00:22:27.917
Um... Ah...

403
00:22:28.087 --> 00:22:30.715
Look. Who's that in the water?

404
00:22:30.890 --> 00:22:33.723
It must be Cody Maverick...

405
00:22:33.893 --> 00:22:37.727
...Pen Gu's favorite surfer.

406
00:22:38.465 --> 00:22:42.866
Did you say Cody Maverick?
Let's go watch him.

407
00:22:43.068 --> 00:22:46.095
- Yeah! Let's go see Cody!
- Yeah!

408
00:22:46.272 --> 00:22:49.002
So have you done
a lot of acting before?

409
00:22:49.175 --> 00:22:52.805
Um, yes. I'm more of a Method actor.

410
00:22:52.980 --> 00:22:56.677
And I think Arnold comes
from a Broadway background.

411
00:22:56.883 --> 00:23:00.248
# I am the very model
Of a modern major general #

412
00:23:00.418 --> 00:23:01.476
# I've information... # #

413
00:23:06.459 --> 00:23:09.122
Here we go. Showtime.

414
00:23:16.268 --> 00:23:18.030
Whoa! All right!

415
00:23:21.641 --> 00:23:22.938
Sick.

416
00:23:24.043 --> 00:23:25.601
Whoo!

417
00:23:27.280 --> 00:23:28.973
Kid's got style.

418
00:23:31.850 --> 00:23:33.182
Nice moves, kid.

419
00:23:33.352 --> 00:23:36.219
Yo, Mr. McMahon,
what about we bring Cody too?

420
00:23:36.422 --> 00:23:37.855
Let's see what else he's got.

421
00:23:38.057 --> 00:23:41.288
What? We already said
we were bringing my girl Lani.

422
00:23:41.494 --> 00:23:43.323
I wanna bring the chicken.

423
00:23:43.527 --> 00:23:45.689
In case I get hungry.

424
00:23:45.930 --> 00:23:48.558
That's cool. I gotta warn you, though...

425
00:23:48.733 --> 00:23:49.859
...I'm not a great cook.

426
00:23:50.035 --> 00:23:52.231
- All right, all right, all right.
- Not so fast.

427
00:23:52.438 --> 00:23:54.303
Tank is the one you want.

428
00:23:54.507 --> 00:23:56.805
I heard you're looking for
a champion to join you.

429
00:23:56.976 --> 00:23:58.806
So I brought my resume.

430
00:23:59.210 --> 00:24:03.647
I like your style.
Reminds me of myself at a younger age.

431
00:24:03.815 --> 00:24:06.181
Well, thanks. But, you know...

432
00:24:06.351 --> 00:24:08.478
...I'm not as handsome as you are, sir.

433
00:24:08.653 --> 00:24:11.350
Ha. Of course not. Oops!

434
00:24:11.557 --> 00:24:12.954
Oh, Briana!

435
00:24:13.157 --> 00:24:16.025
- Sorry about that.
- Oh, that's good.

436
00:24:16.194 --> 00:24:20.358
You better take that. Who made
this thing? My trophies never broke.

437
00:24:20.532 --> 00:24:23.024
- Oh! Again.
- Ridiculous. That thing's garbage.

438
00:24:23.202 --> 00:24:25.192
- Take it. Take the whole thing back.
- Funny.

439
00:24:25.370 --> 00:24:29.237
Well, now I have more of her,
so thanks.

440
00:24:29.406 --> 00:24:33.536
This is my guy. Everybody else
has a guy. I want a guy.

441
00:24:33.745 --> 00:24:35.235
Oh, for crying out loud.

442
00:24:35.413 --> 00:24:37.381
Fine. You can keep your rookies.

443
00:24:37.549 --> 00:24:40.041
- Yes! Up top! Headbutt!
- Yes! Ooh!

444
00:24:40.219 --> 00:24:43.050
- Awesome.
- Yeah, I love those.

445
00:24:43.253 --> 00:24:46.745
But they're your responsibility. You've
gotta show them how we do things.

446
00:24:48.292 --> 00:24:51.386
We're gonna challenge you
on all aspects of what we do.

447
00:24:51.595 --> 00:24:54.258
Power, speed,
endurance and teamwork.

448
00:24:54.432 --> 00:24:56.992
May the best mentor-rookie team win.

449
00:24:57.602 --> 00:24:59.796
Bring it on, fool.

450
00:25:00.037 --> 00:25:03.939
Well, obviously Lani and I will win.
Let's do this.

451
00:25:04.309 --> 00:25:06.277
Do you know how to surf?

452
00:25:06.444 --> 00:25:08.435
Dude, I'm a star.

453
00:25:08.613 --> 00:25:10.274
Okay, we're in.

454
00:25:10.482 --> 00:25:12.541
All right. Then that's the way
it's gonna be.

455
00:25:14.250 --> 00:25:18.051
If your guy or girl dies or gets hurt and
I have to carry them all the way back...

456
00:25:18.222 --> 00:25:20.952
...I'm gonna make you
scrub the whale for a year!

457
00:25:21.525 --> 00:25:24.927
All aboard! Next stop, Slaughter island.

458
00:25:25.597 --> 00:25:28.223
So how much did you pay
to bribe those kids?

459
00:25:28.398 --> 00:25:31.128
- Three shells apiece.
- You're such a dork.

460
00:25:31.301 --> 00:25:34.235
Not to mention a failure.
Ha, ha, ha, ha!

461
00:25:34.404 --> 00:25:36.065
When I become one of the Hang 5...

462
00:25:36.240 --> 00:25:38.572
...I'm gonna come back
and crush your surf school.

463
00:25:38.742 --> 00:25:43.303
All your students will be mine.
And they'll be happy. Ha, ha, ha, ha!

464
00:25:43.546 --> 00:25:46.846
- Like me.
- We can't let him win, Cody.

465
00:25:47.050 --> 00:25:49.953
Don't worry. I got this.

466
00:25:53.458 --> 00:25:56.358
Can't this thing go a little slower?

467
00:25:58.093 --> 00:25:59.789
Where would be the fun in that?

468
00:25:59.996 --> 00:26:03.693
We're passing through some
rough waters. It's safer to go fast.

469
00:26:03.966 --> 00:26:05.195
Aaah!

470
00:26:05.369 --> 00:26:06.996
Joe!

471
00:26:07.671 --> 00:26:08.968
Thanks, man.

472
00:26:09.139 --> 00:26:11.973
Almost lost my lunch.

473
00:26:12.143 --> 00:26:14.109
Say no more, Under-bro.

474
00:26:14.277 --> 00:26:17.610
I can hold your hair if you need to yak.

475
00:26:24.354 --> 00:26:26.481
This is just amazing.
Can you believe it?

476
00:26:26.657 --> 00:26:29.819
I'm traveling to the Trenches
with the Hang 5. Ha, ha!

477
00:26:29.992 --> 00:26:32.392
Oh, man. Somebody pinch me.

478
00:26:32.829 --> 00:26:34.888
- You're welcome.
- Heh.

479
00:26:39.169 --> 00:26:41.535
Look, I'm a diva, I'll admit it.

480
00:26:41.705 --> 00:26:43.637
But I'm a power diva.

481
00:26:43.805 --> 00:26:47.036
And I was thinking you fellas
might wanna focus on me more.

482
00:26:47.210 --> 00:26:50.646
We could do a spinoff, Power Diva.

483
00:26:50.847 --> 00:26:54.477
A crime-fighting surfing puff. In
with a bad attitude...

484
00:26:54.651 --> 00:26:56.050
...and a thirst for action.

485
00:26:56.486 --> 00:27:00.182
Oh, it's got blockbuster
written all over it.

486
00:27:01.724 --> 00:27:04.191
# Is gonna stop me now # #

487
00:27:10.900 --> 00:27:12.732
We're almost there.

488
00:27:12.936 --> 00:27:17.371
How can you tell? This fog is so thick,
I can barely see anything.

489
00:27:17.907 --> 00:27:19.772
My shell told me.

490
00:27:20.276 --> 00:27:22.744
It's a map that talks.

491
00:27:22.945 --> 00:27:26.540
What's wrong, bro?
Don't you believe in magic?

492
00:27:26.849 --> 00:27:31.683
We'll be there in four, three, two, one.

493
00:27:31.853 --> 00:27:33.081
Look.

494
00:27:37.526 --> 00:27:39.050
Gnarly.

495
00:27:39.362 --> 00:27:42.924
It's so beautiful.

496
00:27:43.398 --> 00:27:45.263
Are we here? Is this it?

497
00:27:45.433 --> 00:27:48.266
No, we're at the edge
of Slaughter island.

498
00:27:48.470 --> 00:27:52.270
The Trenches is hidden here
somewhere. We're going to find it.

499
00:27:52.741 --> 00:27:57.270
Forward, ever forward,
our intrepid team presses on...

500
00:27:57.446 --> 00:28:01.541
...woefully unaware that no penguin
has ever ventured into the Trenches...

501
00:28:01.716 --> 00:28:04.207
...and lived to tell the story.

502
00:28:07.890 --> 00:28:10.289
Looks like this is
as far as the whale goes.

503
00:28:10.492 --> 00:28:12.961
I got your board for you, Mr. Hunter.
Right here.

504
00:28:13.129 --> 00:28:15.595
- Thanks, Hank.
- It's Tank. It's Tank.

505
00:28:15.763 --> 00:28:17.390
Know what? Hank's better, actually.

506
00:28:17.598 --> 00:28:19.294
- Next stop, RTL!
- RTL!

507
00:28:19.467 --> 00:28:20.729
RTL!

508
00:28:20.936 --> 00:28:22.665
Did they tell you what RTL means?

509
00:28:22.837 --> 00:28:25.068
It means "race the losers."

510
00:28:25.241 --> 00:28:26.435
Let's get that guy.

511
00:28:31.913 --> 00:28:36.349
Hey, excuse me.
Can you take me back to Pen Gu?

512
00:28:36.518 --> 00:28:39.510
I think I left my sunblock.

513
00:28:39.721 --> 00:28:41.279
Come on.

514
00:28:41.623 --> 00:28:43.958
Dude!

515
00:29:16.357 --> 00:29:19.326
Whoa! Look at that.

516
00:29:19.493 --> 00:29:22.485
Killer view, bro.

517
00:29:22.896 --> 00:29:24.329
Hey, rookies!

518
00:29:24.531 --> 00:29:25.760
We're down here!

519
00:29:26.267 --> 00:29:28.665
Whoo! Yeah! Yes!

520
00:29:32.406 --> 00:29:35.204
Oh, my gosh, you can surf on this stuff.

521
00:29:35.409 --> 00:29:37.036
Dude, what is this?

522
00:29:40.080 --> 00:29:43.049
The taste of death.

523
00:29:43.218 --> 00:29:46.583
This is crushed whale bones.

524
00:29:46.853 --> 00:29:48.650
I should move here.

525
00:29:48.855 --> 00:29:51.381
The conch is telling me
we have to keep moving.

526
00:29:51.558 --> 00:29:54.288
This place is dangerous.
So let's head out.

527
00:29:54.495 --> 00:29:55.861
What's so dangerous about it?

528
00:29:56.831 --> 00:29:59.559
Hold on. What's that, conch?

529
00:29:59.732 --> 00:30:01.256
Okay, I'll tell him.

530
00:30:01.435 --> 00:30:03.902
Conch says, shut up!

531
00:30:04.203 --> 00:30:05.329
- Heh, heh.
- Hey.

532
00:30:05.538 --> 00:30:09.600
From up here it looks like the sand pit
will take us straight into the island.

533
00:30:09.843 --> 00:30:12.744
That'll save us a ton of time.
How about a race?

534
00:30:12.913 --> 00:30:15.904
Last team to the bottom
waxes all our boards tonight.

535
00:30:16.115 --> 00:30:18.811
You're on, fool.
Cody and I are gonna smoke you.

536
00:30:19.018 --> 00:30:20.953
Yeah, Tank. You're going down.

537
00:30:21.188 --> 00:30:25.089
Ohh, I'm so scared. Not.

538
00:30:25.425 --> 00:30:27.621
Ha! Me and Lani will take you on.

539
00:30:27.828 --> 00:30:30.727
And as always, it'll be ladies first!

540
00:30:30.929 --> 00:30:33.865
Me and the chicken are in too.
Where is he?

541
00:30:34.033 --> 00:30:37.025
Hey, don't take this the wrong way...

542
00:30:37.203 --> 00:30:39.798
...but didn't you used to be taller?

543
00:30:39.973 --> 00:30:42.441
Oh, my gosh,
you're standing in quicksand!

544
00:30:42.609 --> 00:30:45.634
Cody, Lani, J.C., help!

545
00:30:47.646 --> 00:30:49.477
Lani, pull!

546
00:30:49.648 --> 00:30:52.743
I'm trying. He's like a boulder.

547
00:30:52.919 --> 00:30:54.045
I got this.

548
00:30:54.220 --> 00:30:56.382
Come on, big guy.
Let's get you out of there.

549
00:30:58.459 --> 00:31:00.118
How much do you weigh?

550
00:31:00.358 --> 00:31:03.055
- Hunter, help me look for the chicken.
- Already on it.

551
00:31:03.796 --> 00:31:06.856
I found him.
There, by that rock. To your right.

552
00:31:07.066 --> 00:31:08.762
Hunh! Gotcha.

553
00:31:10.303 --> 00:31:14.295
Am I dead? Are you my father?

554
00:31:16.608 --> 00:31:17.870
Come on!

555
00:31:28.522 --> 00:31:30.818
Come on! Come on!

556
00:31:31.323 --> 00:31:32.813
Aah!

557
00:31:33.091 --> 00:31:34.991
Yeah! Go, J.C.

558
00:31:35.160 --> 00:31:38.186
Ha, ha! That's how it's done.

559
00:31:38.598 --> 00:31:40.759
Wow, J.C. Perfect form.

560
00:31:40.967 --> 00:31:43.492
- Thanks, kid.
- Very impressive.

561
00:31:43.667 --> 00:31:45.659
You gonna put me down now?

562
00:31:45.904 --> 00:31:49.101
You're lucky it's leg day.
I'm just gonna sneak in a quick set.

563
00:31:53.012 --> 00:31:56.640
- Thanks, show-off.
- Any time.

564
00:31:57.316 --> 00:31:59.509
Leg-pressing a large, heavy boulder.

565
00:31:59.683 --> 00:32:01.480
Then onto a one-handed handstand...

566
00:32:01.652 --> 00:32:04.315
...all while
still leg-pressing the boulder.

567
00:32:04.489 --> 00:32:06.514
The secret to my amazing physique?

568
00:32:06.691 --> 00:32:09.684
Eat right, exercise and never give up...

569
00:32:09.862 --> 00:32:12.558
...on being awesome.

570
00:32:14.698 --> 00:32:16.360
Hang 5, let's do this!

571
00:32:19.837 --> 00:32:22.568
- All right!
- Yeah! Yeah, dude!

572
00:32:25.076 --> 00:32:28.535
Let's see how these wave jockeys
perform on the dunes.

573
00:32:28.714 --> 00:32:31.146
They have not put in the hours
shredding the sand...

574
00:32:31.315 --> 00:32:34.012
...but, wow, folks,
they're putting on quite a show.

575
00:32:34.219 --> 00:32:36.050
I make this look good.

576
00:32:36.221 --> 00:32:38.985
- Yeah!
- Bring it!

577
00:32:39.191 --> 00:32:41.216
Check this out.

578
00:32:41.693 --> 00:32:43.160
Nice moves, Paige.

579
00:32:43.328 --> 00:32:45.488
- All right.
- We do it old-school.

580
00:32:45.696 --> 00:32:48.187
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

581
00:32:51.101 --> 00:32:54.401
- Lani, I see a shortcut.
- Right behind you.

582
00:32:54.906 --> 00:32:57.204
Ho, ho! In your face, Hunter.

583
00:32:59.777 --> 00:33:01.574
Whee!

584
00:33:03.012 --> 00:33:04.878
Rest in peace.

585
00:33:05.749 --> 00:33:07.512
Yeah.

586
00:33:11.356 --> 00:33:12.380
Whoa!

587
00:33:12.591 --> 00:33:14.352
Ho-ho!

588
00:33:14.791 --> 00:33:16.191
Yeah!

589
00:33:17.528 --> 00:33:20.793
- Bye, J.C.
- Ha, ha, ha. Aw...

590
00:33:21.232 --> 00:33:22.393
This is it.

591
00:33:24.202 --> 00:33:26.761
- Eat my dust, Tank.
- Oh, that's what you think.

592
00:33:27.906 --> 00:33:30.771
- Whoa!
- Ha-ha-ha!

593
00:33:34.378 --> 00:33:36.938
Sand's the best!

594
00:33:37.815 --> 00:33:39.407
Cody!

595
00:33:43.255 --> 00:33:47.213
- You still with me, bro?
- Yeah. I think so.

596
00:33:47.424 --> 00:33:49.152
Ha, ha, ha, awesome.

597
00:33:49.325 --> 00:33:51.816
- Paige, we finished first. I can't believe it.
- Yeah!

598
00:33:52.028 --> 00:33:53.496
That was incredible.

599
00:33:53.664 --> 00:33:56.030
Ho, ho, ho, unh!

600
00:34:05.409 --> 00:34:07.536
That tickled.

601
00:34:08.646 --> 00:34:11.080
- Great job out there, Lani.
- Ha, ha, ha!

602
00:34:11.248 --> 00:34:13.239
Thanks. That was a lot of fun.

603
00:34:13.417 --> 00:34:14.746
Gotta hand it to you, Paige.

604
00:34:14.916 --> 00:34:17.317
You got me good
when you banked off that rib cage...

605
00:34:17.487 --> 00:34:20.752
- ...and landed in front of me.
- I've got a few tricks you haven't seen.

606
00:34:20.923 --> 00:34:22.755
Hey. Check it out.

607
00:34:25.663 --> 00:34:29.962
Hey, flattop. What happened?
You take the scenic route?

608
00:34:30.133 --> 00:34:33.101
Heh, heh. Yeah, you know me.
I'm just a bit of a tourist.

609
00:34:33.268 --> 00:34:34.600
I like to take in the sights.

610
00:34:34.771 --> 00:34:38.002
Remember,
I like a nice high gloss on my board.

611
00:34:38.174 --> 00:34:40.700
Don't get too comfortable.
I'll get you back.

612
00:34:40.878 --> 00:34:43.142
That was quite a spill
you took out there.

613
00:34:43.314 --> 00:34:44.802
How does my dust taste?

614
00:34:44.980 --> 00:34:46.379
You cut me off, you cheater.

615
00:34:46.581 --> 00:34:49.346
Oh? I don't know
what you're talking about.

616
00:34:49.585 --> 00:34:51.519
- I'd never do anything to hurt you.
- Hey!

617
00:34:51.688 --> 00:34:53.486
You should learn
to stay out of my way.

618
00:34:53.657 --> 00:34:56.056
I'm gonna join the Hang 5,
no matter what.

619
00:34:56.225 --> 00:34:59.887
How badly you want to lose
is entirely up to you.

620
00:35:03.332 --> 00:35:04.492
Grrr...

621
00:35:06.369 --> 00:35:09.998
That Tank guy is ridiculous.
He's like a cartoon villain.

622
00:35:10.173 --> 00:35:12.506
Why did you let Hunter bring him?

623
00:35:12.676 --> 00:35:15.302
Everyone is here for a reason.

624
00:35:15.477 --> 00:35:18.878
I want to see how
the rest of the newbies deal with him.

625
00:35:19.047 --> 00:35:21.379
You still think Cody has what it takes?

626
00:35:21.616 --> 00:35:24.085
Look, Mr. McMahon,
I know he wiped out out there...

627
00:35:24.253 --> 00:35:26.312
...but he's a good surfer.
Give him a chance.

628
00:35:26.489 --> 00:35:28.980
I'm not talking about surfing.
I've been watching him.

629
00:35:29.157 --> 00:35:32.718
I think he's a bit of a hothead.
He might want this too much.

630
00:35:32.928 --> 00:35:35.420
Don't worry about it.
He's just like me at that age.

631
00:35:35.631 --> 00:35:36.620
He'll be cool.

632
00:35:37.066 --> 00:35:39.702
All right, we'll see.

633
00:35:41.437 --> 00:35:43.234
Okay, okay. I've got one.

634
00:35:43.439 --> 00:35:47.203
What did the wave say to the surfer?

635
00:35:47.409 --> 00:35:48.569
Oh, what?

636
00:35:48.777 --> 00:35:50.904
Have a swell time!

637
00:35:53.382 --> 00:35:54.441
Get it, huh?

638
00:35:54.684 --> 00:35:56.049
Have a swell time.

639
00:35:56.219 --> 00:35:59.745
Oh, ha, ha, swell. Ha, ha, ha.

640
00:35:59.921 --> 00:36:01.855
Oh, that was good. Swell.

641
00:36:02.023 --> 00:36:06.619
Oh, Mr. McMahon, that's like
the greatest surfing joke maybe ever.

642
00:36:06.795 --> 00:36:08.922
So good. Unh!

643
00:36:09.731 --> 00:36:10.720
Thank you.

644
00:36:10.899 --> 00:36:14.459
What do you call a surfer
that just broke up with his girlfriend?

645
00:36:14.935 --> 00:36:16.630
Homeless!

646
00:36:22.911 --> 00:36:27.245
Dude, Cody. We're just trying to
wax the boards, not set them on fire.

647
00:36:27.416 --> 00:36:30.179
You're gonna burn a hole in that thing.

648
00:36:30.384 --> 00:36:32.409
Tank cheated.
He knocked me off my board.

649
00:36:32.586 --> 00:36:33.610
That's why we lost.

650
00:36:33.821 --> 00:36:37.690
Yeah? I didn't see anything. You sure?

651
00:36:37.893 --> 00:36:40.987
He totally rubbed it in my face.
He practically admitted to it.

652
00:36:41.229 --> 00:36:42.959
That's messed up.
But you know what?

653
00:36:43.199 --> 00:36:46.894
Maybe let it go. It's not worth
getting all bent out of shape about.

654
00:36:47.067 --> 00:36:51.561
We had an awesome day, right?
Were those dunes gnarly or what?

655
00:36:51.739 --> 00:36:53.900
Yeah. That was pretty epic.

656
00:36:54.074 --> 00:36:56.976
And I got to ride with you guys.
It still feels pretty surreal.

657
00:36:57.145 --> 00:37:00.135
I mean, like, I can't believe
this is actually my life right now.

658
00:37:00.314 --> 00:37:04.273
I just... I just wish
that I hadn't let you down.

659
00:37:05.085 --> 00:37:07.680
Let me down?
What are you talking about?

660
00:37:07.856 --> 00:37:10.790
Look, man.
There are plenty of jerks out there.

661
00:37:10.958 --> 00:37:14.688
If it's not Tank, it'll be somebody else.
Just take the high road.

662
00:37:14.861 --> 00:37:18.491
You'll be a lot happier, I promise.

663
00:37:19.300 --> 00:37:21.825
All right, man. You got it.

664
00:37:23.103 --> 00:37:24.263
- Ha, ha!
- Pull.

665
00:37:24.438 --> 00:37:25.872
- Pull.
- Whoo!

666
00:37:26.107 --> 00:37:29.734
- Pull. Pull.
- All right!

667
00:37:29.943 --> 00:37:33.344
- Why are they sleeping up there?
- Mmm...

668
00:37:33.546 --> 00:37:35.309
Maybe they don't like us.

669
00:37:35.482 --> 00:37:39.214
I bet it's a tribal thing, you know?
Paying homage to the surfing gods.

670
00:37:39.386 --> 00:37:41.320
Wrong. None of the above.

671
00:37:41.489 --> 00:37:43.321
It's actually for protection.

672
00:37:43.525 --> 00:37:45.616
Protection? From what?

673
00:37:45.825 --> 00:37:50.695
This is Slaughter island. Who knows
what's creeping around at night?

674
00:37:52.566 --> 00:37:55.400
And you're gonna want to
plant that board a bit deeper, bro.

675
00:37:55.570 --> 00:37:57.230
- Oh!
- Ha, ha, ha...

676
00:37:57.404 --> 00:38:00.166
You guys sleep up in the nosebleeds
if you want to.

677
00:38:00.339 --> 00:38:03.503
Tank Evans is not scared
of some little forest critters.

678
00:38:03.676 --> 00:38:07.010
Neither is my main girl Michelle.
Isn't that right, baby?

679
00:38:07.181 --> 00:38:10.207
Big Daddy won't let anything harm you.

680
00:38:12.386 --> 00:38:14.649
This is Michelle.

681
00:38:14.821 --> 00:38:18.312
We've been together for about...
What is it, babe?... Three years now.

682
00:38:18.490 --> 00:38:20.254
I bought her at a garage sale.

683
00:38:20.426 --> 00:38:25.056
I saw her from across the lawn.
I was like, "Oh, yeah."

684
00:38:25.232 --> 00:38:27.530
Don't get me wrong,
I still ride other boards.

685
00:38:27.701 --> 00:38:32.296
But... But, Michelle, she's special.

686
00:38:32.939 --> 00:38:35.373
Hey, Tank.
Does Michelle have a friend?

687
00:38:35.542 --> 00:38:38.239
Yeah? Well, we're not scared either.

688
00:38:38.412 --> 00:38:42.006
- Yeah. If you're fine with it, I am.
- I ain't afraid of no forest critters.

689
00:38:42.181 --> 00:38:43.740
- Totally cool.
- Okay. Yep.

690
00:38:43.918 --> 00:38:46.180
So we're all fine down here.
Oof!

691
00:38:46.351 --> 00:38:49.515
Well, you all sleep tight then.

692
00:38:49.722 --> 00:38:52.054
Don't let the bed bugs bite.

693
00:38:52.258 --> 00:38:53.589
Oh, we won't.

694
00:38:53.760 --> 00:38:57.197
And the bed bugs will bite you.

695
00:38:58.599 --> 00:39:00.121
Uh...

696
00:39:27.160 --> 00:39:31.151
Don't hate me, man.
I'm just polishing my trophy.

697
00:39:39.739 --> 00:39:42.401
I think I just laid an egg.

698
00:39:42.575 --> 00:39:44.373
I didn't forget about you, babe.

699
00:39:47.512 --> 00:39:49.138
Oh!

700
00:39:55.253 --> 00:39:56.346
Whoa!

701
00:39:56.522 --> 00:39:57.853
Nice hang time.

702
00:39:59.890 --> 00:40:00.914
Cody?

703
00:40:27.820 --> 00:40:31.117
Congratulations. You're dead.
Ha, ha!

704
00:40:31.322 --> 00:40:32.346
What?

705
00:40:33.724 --> 00:40:38.161
That's what happens when you
don't work together in a place like this.

706
00:40:38.362 --> 00:40:40.160
Wait, wait, wait. This was a test?

707
00:40:40.332 --> 00:40:44.325
It was. We wanted to see
how well you work under pressure.

708
00:40:44.935 --> 00:40:49.031
Never split up. Understand?
You stick together, no matter what.

709
00:40:49.206 --> 00:40:52.176
When you're a team,
you always have each other's backs.

710
00:40:52.344 --> 00:40:53.936
Got it?

711
00:40:56.048 --> 00:40:58.812
Well, all things considered,
not bad for your first time.

712
00:40:58.984 --> 00:41:02.918
At least none of you peed your pants.
Right, Hunter? Ha, ha, ha!

713
00:41:04.321 --> 00:41:07.484
I told you guys, I sat in a puddle.

714
00:41:07.692 --> 00:41:09.160
- Oh, yeah.
- All right!

715
00:41:09.327 --> 00:41:12.660
Don't worry, Hunter, bro.
I peed my pants too.

716
00:41:12.864 --> 00:41:14.525
- I don't have any pants...
- Let's go!

717
00:41:14.700 --> 00:41:16.394
...so I mostly just peed on my feet.

718
00:41:16.667 --> 00:41:21.195
I bet you thought it was me
making all that noise. Didn't you?

719
00:41:24.208 --> 00:41:28.747
Yeah. You don't wanna mess with me
when I'm in a bad mood.

720
00:41:53.370 --> 00:41:55.031
Can't sleep?

721
00:41:55.406 --> 00:41:58.808
Yeah, I think I need a minute
to calm down from all the excitement.

722
00:41:59.943 --> 00:42:01.774
My heart's jumping out of my chest.

723
00:42:01.945 --> 00:42:03.879
Yeah, I can imagine.

724
00:42:04.047 --> 00:42:06.140
This has been some day.

725
00:42:06.316 --> 00:42:08.443
Must be a pretty big deal to you.

726
00:42:08.651 --> 00:42:11.883
This is my dream, Lani.
I can't stop thinking about it.

727
00:42:12.056 --> 00:42:13.956
I don't think I blinked once all day.

728
00:42:14.125 --> 00:42:16.149
I didn't wanna miss a second.

729
00:42:21.431 --> 00:42:24.993
Mr. McMahon thinks you're
amazing. He's totally gonna pick you.

730
00:42:25.169 --> 00:42:27.636
I don't know.

731
00:42:27.804 --> 00:42:31.967
I miss Pen Gu.
We've been gone for so long.

732
00:42:32.141 --> 00:42:35.134
I can't wait to tell our friends back home
about all of this.

733
00:42:35.478 --> 00:42:37.605
Heh, heh.
Yeah. They'll never believe it.

734
00:42:37.781 --> 00:42:39.339
I wish every day was like this.

735
00:42:39.582 --> 00:42:42.984
I feel like I'm finally living the life
I've always wanted to, you know?

736
00:42:43.154 --> 00:42:45.279
I wish this feeling could last forever.

737
00:42:45.454 --> 00:42:46.479
Heh.

738
00:42:46.656 --> 00:42:49.021
Yeah, well, you still gotta sleep.

739
00:42:49.191 --> 00:42:53.492
Yeah, in a minute.
Let's soak this in a while longer.

740
00:43:14.651 --> 00:43:16.446
Uh...

741
00:43:18.387 --> 00:43:19.581
Uh!

742
00:43:26.029 --> 00:43:28.497
Cock-a-doodle-dude!

743
00:43:30.899 --> 00:43:33.834
Cock-a-doodle-shut up!

744
00:43:45.913 --> 00:43:47.905
I slept like a corpse.

745
00:43:52.554 --> 00:43:54.887
Come on, guys.
We've got a lot of ground to cover.

746
00:43:55.058 --> 00:43:56.991
Remember what we talked about
last night.

747
00:43:57.159 --> 00:44:00.594
After all, this journey isn't just about
getting to the Trenches.

748
00:44:00.761 --> 00:44:03.821
One of you will be replacing me
on the Hang 5.

749
00:44:03.998 --> 00:44:09.062
Those are some big shoes to fill,
so show me you've got big feet.

750
00:44:12.075 --> 00:44:14.543
Yeah.

751
00:44:14.944 --> 00:44:16.773
It says there's supposed to be
a bridge.

752
00:44:16.944 --> 00:44:18.242
- Boss! Stop!
- Mr. McMahon!

753
00:44:18.413 --> 00:44:19.538
- Wait, wait.
- Come back!

754
00:44:19.714 --> 00:44:21.375
- Rerouting.
- Look where you're going!

755
00:44:21.549 --> 00:44:23.210
- What's that mean?
- Don't go further!

756
00:44:23.385 --> 00:44:25.216
Hey, what's the holdup?

757
00:44:28.957 --> 00:44:30.924
Ha, ha! You're afraid of heights?

758
00:44:32.059 --> 00:44:33.253
Oh, yeah!

759
00:44:42.237 --> 00:44:45.035
Let's have some fun.
I bet you can't get past me.

760
00:44:48.276 --> 00:44:50.244
Oh, you're on.

761
00:44:50.745 --> 00:44:52.440
Whoa, whoa!

762
00:44:54.283 --> 00:44:58.583
Perfectly matched.
This is truly a clash of the titans.

763
00:45:02.723 --> 00:45:04.622
Yeah! Show them
how you do it, Mr. Hunter.

764
00:45:04.791 --> 00:45:07.056
You see that?
He blew right past your guy.

765
00:45:07.228 --> 00:45:08.286
Come on, J.C.

766
00:45:08.963 --> 00:45:10.157
Oh, yeah?

767
00:45:12.301 --> 00:45:13.962
- Yeah!
- Whoo! Ha-ha.

768
00:45:14.136 --> 00:45:16.068
Yeah, he showed Hunter what's up.

769
00:45:16.269 --> 00:45:18.397
- Come on, Lani.
- Whoa. Yeah!

770
00:45:18.572 --> 00:45:20.267
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

771
00:45:20.574 --> 00:45:21.802
Yeah! Whoo!

772
00:45:21.976 --> 00:45:24.138
Ha-ha-ha.
Nice, Lani. Way to go.

773
00:45:24.313 --> 00:45:26.678
Oh, that's cool, but...

774
00:45:31.017 --> 00:45:32.951
Come on, wimp. It's our turn.

775
00:45:33.119 --> 00:45:35.349
Hope you don't fall to your death
or anything.

776
00:45:38.092 --> 00:45:39.855
Whoa, whoa!

777
00:45:43.131 --> 00:45:44.496
Can you do this?

778
00:45:44.666 --> 00:45:46.359
- Cut it out!
- Ls this bothering you?

779
00:45:46.533 --> 00:45:47.830
Is this bothering you? This?

780
00:45:48.001 --> 00:45:51.801
Cody Maverick looks like
he's in real trouble. I can't look.

781
00:45:52.005 --> 00:45:54.941
Ha, ha!
Try not to look so scared in front of J.C.

782
00:45:56.477 --> 00:45:58.809
Tank, seriously, stop. Whoa, whoa.
Okay, okay.

783
00:45:58.980 --> 00:46:01.243
- Dude, come on.
- This is fun.

784
00:46:01.748 --> 00:46:03.375
Uhn!

785
00:46:11.858 --> 00:46:14.487
- No, I'm good. That was my plan.
- Yeah!

786
00:46:14.695 --> 00:46:16.388
That was gnarly.

787
00:46:16.662 --> 00:46:18.722
- Oh... Oh!
- Cody, no!

788
00:46:25.573 --> 00:46:28.474
- Look out!
- Wait for me, guys!

789
00:46:41.321 --> 00:46:42.686
You okay, Cody?

790
00:46:42.857 --> 00:46:43.846
Yeah.

791
00:46:44.025 --> 00:46:48.016
Fortunately, this solid stone floor
was here to break my fall.

792
00:46:48.394 --> 00:46:50.329
Where are the others?

793
00:46:54.300 --> 00:46:55.734
Whoa.

794
00:46:56.903 --> 00:46:59.929
Looks like
we're in some kind of a tomb.

795
00:47:00.306 --> 00:47:05.538
Yeah. Whoever these people were,
they really loved surfing.

796
00:47:06.178 --> 00:47:08.807
I think these little symbols
mean something.

797
00:47:09.716 --> 00:47:11.013
Maybe it's a story.

798
00:47:11.217 --> 00:47:12.241
Yeah, see?

799
00:47:12.419 --> 00:47:16.354
This one's about a guy
who surfed a wave as tall as a mountain.

800
00:47:17.389 --> 00:47:19.357
And this one
shows a guy surfing on sand.

801
00:47:19.525 --> 00:47:22.255
- We did that.
- Hey, check it out.

802
00:47:22.428 --> 00:47:24.589
Whoa. What does it say?

803
00:47:24.763 --> 00:47:27.756
It looks like
the story of a young penguin.

804
00:47:27.934 --> 00:47:30.459
Pretty good surfer, got some fans.

805
00:47:30.635 --> 00:47:33.264
Yeah, definitely looks like
things were going his way.

806
00:47:33.739 --> 00:47:35.536
Yeah, yeah, and then?

807
00:47:35.707 --> 00:47:38.370
Oh! He got eaten by a bunch of sharks.

808
00:47:38.545 --> 00:47:41.378
- Oh! Okay.
- Whoa.

809
00:47:41.581 --> 00:47:42.911
This guy surfed through fire?

810
00:47:43.115 --> 00:47:44.879
Dude, that's hardcore.

811
00:47:45.085 --> 00:47:49.486
Hey, this isn't a tomb.
It's a surfer's hall of fame.

812
00:47:50.355 --> 00:47:53.722
Oh, man. This is so awesome. Wow!

813
00:47:54.960 --> 00:47:57.156
Do you think people
will remember you like that?

814
00:47:57.363 --> 00:48:00.332
A legendary surfer
who did all these amazing things?

815
00:48:00.500 --> 00:48:03.127
Jeez, I hope not.

816
00:48:03.368 --> 00:48:05.631
Really? What?
What are you talking about?

817
00:48:05.803 --> 00:48:07.293
This is what I've always wanted.

818
00:48:07.472 --> 00:48:09.839
To be remembered as a legend,
somebody respected.

819
00:48:10.008 --> 00:48:11.407
You know, like a real winner.

820
00:48:11.810 --> 00:48:16.610
Not me. I want to be remembered
for who I am, not what I did.

821
00:48:16.781 --> 00:48:18.976
Look, Cody,
surfing's awesome and all...

822
00:48:19.150 --> 00:48:21.585
...but there are
a lot more important things in life.

823
00:48:21.987 --> 00:48:23.511
You'll see.

824
00:48:23.689 --> 00:48:25.884
I just want to be remembered.

825
00:48:36.100 --> 00:48:38.934
Lani, Lani, it's okay. It's just me, love.

826
00:48:39.104 --> 00:48:40.537
- Paige.
- You all right?

827
00:48:40.706 --> 00:48:42.606
- Yeah.
- Hello?

828
00:48:42.808 --> 00:48:46.834
Cody? Lani? Anyone?

829
00:48:47.011 --> 00:48:48.171
Conch?

830
00:48:48.913 --> 00:48:49.970
Chicken Joe?

831
00:48:50.147 --> 00:48:53.914
It's me.
Oi, over here.

832
00:48:54.118 --> 00:48:55.710
Is everyone okay?

833
00:48:55.920 --> 00:48:57.889
Just me and the big guy.

834
00:48:58.056 --> 00:49:00.818
There's a little doodle
of a door on this wall.

835
00:49:00.991 --> 00:49:03.722
Do you guys see a lever on your side?

836
00:49:03.961 --> 00:49:05.360
I see it.

837
00:49:11.236 --> 00:49:14.865
Whoa! Righteous door.

838
00:49:15.073 --> 00:49:16.971
Are we glad to see you guys.

839
00:49:17.140 --> 00:49:19.301
Come on, let's go.
Our friends might need help.

840
00:49:19.476 --> 00:49:21.945
Stop. This place is dangerous.

841
00:49:26.217 --> 00:49:29.244
There are lost souls
lurking around every corner.

842
00:49:29.655 --> 00:49:34.182
I can feel them. They seem to be
guarding some kind of treasure.

843
00:49:35.759 --> 00:49:39.389
What kind of idiot
would steal from a freaky place like this?

844
00:49:39.597 --> 00:49:43.658
Ha, ha!
I'm rich! I'm rich! Look at how rich I am.

845
00:49:44.001 --> 00:49:46.696
I wonder how much gold
we can pack on the whale.

846
00:49:46.903 --> 00:49:50.395
Let's come back with a bigger whale.
No, 10 whales.

847
00:50:01.784 --> 00:50:03.343
The conch says...

848
00:50:03.520 --> 00:50:05.545
There's no reception in here.

849
00:50:05.722 --> 00:50:08.213
Let me see if I can get any bars.

850
00:50:09.427 --> 00:50:11.054
All right, there we go.

851
00:50:11.295 --> 00:50:15.231
According to the conch, the penguins
on this island used to worship surfing.

852
00:50:15.400 --> 00:50:19.391
We're in the treasure room of their king,
the wealthiest surfer who ever lived.

853
00:50:19.569 --> 00:50:23.699
A rich surfer?
Now I've seen everything.

854
00:50:23.873 --> 00:50:25.500
Mmm...

855
00:50:28.045 --> 00:50:30.445
Michelle, we have had
some good times together...

856
00:50:30.615 --> 00:50:34.983
...but I think we both know
Tank Evans deserves better.

857
00:50:35.151 --> 00:50:38.587
Don't worry. It's not me, it's you.

858
00:50:38.755 --> 00:50:41.748
Time to hit the road, babe.
Tank needs an upgrade.

859
00:50:41.959 --> 00:50:46.326
Hold on a second. The conch tells me
this place is booby-trapped like crazy.

860
00:50:46.528 --> 00:50:49.224
We take anything, we die.

861
00:50:49.398 --> 00:50:51.731
What? That's too bad.

862
00:50:51.901 --> 00:50:54.426
Well, I didn't get into this
for the money.

863
00:50:54.604 --> 00:50:56.162
Easy come, easy go.

864
00:50:56.339 --> 00:50:59.002
Hey, Tank. Did you hear that?
Don't touch anything.

865
00:50:59.176 --> 00:51:00.643
This place is booby-trapped.

866
00:51:00.811 --> 00:51:02.777
Say what?

867
00:51:04.847 --> 00:51:07.475
Michelle! How could you?

868
00:51:07.783 --> 00:51:09.250
- We've gotta get out.
- Let's go!

869
00:51:12.589 --> 00:51:14.113
- What's happening?
- I don't know.

870
00:51:14.291 --> 00:51:16.417
But let's not wait around to find out.

871
00:51:17.593 --> 00:51:19.823
An old aqueduct.
That must lead outside.

872
00:51:19.995 --> 00:51:22.931
Come on, Cody. It's our only shot.

873
00:51:30.607 --> 00:51:33.096
Oh, yeah! Ha-ha-ha.

874
00:51:39.148 --> 00:51:42.380
- Watch out for the darts!
- Shield yourself with your board.

875
00:51:42.819 --> 00:51:44.218
Stay together.

876
00:51:44.454 --> 00:51:45.853
Oh, look out!

877
00:51:46.022 --> 00:51:47.215
Ow!

878
00:51:48.991 --> 00:51:50.480
Aagh!

879
00:51:53.595 --> 00:51:54.584
Oh!

880
00:51:54.763 --> 00:51:58.324
- Which way do we go?
- Follow me. The conch knows the way.

881
00:52:06.008 --> 00:52:07.498
I hope Cody made it out.

882
00:52:07.676 --> 00:52:11.875
Don't worry, love.
If we made it out, they'll be fine.

883
00:52:14.016 --> 00:52:16.643
I love all you guys.

884
00:52:16.851 --> 00:52:18.375
Are you okay, big guy?

885
00:52:18.553 --> 00:52:21.818
I feel very peaceful.

886
00:52:21.989 --> 00:52:24.151
Must be the acupuncture.

887
00:52:27.629 --> 00:52:30.929
- That's a pretty posh board, Tank.
- What?

888
00:52:31.167 --> 00:52:33.156
- You didn't take that, did you?
- No, no, no.

889
00:52:33.334 --> 00:52:34.824
This is my old board. It just...

890
00:52:35.002 --> 00:52:37.994
Why all the fighting?

891
00:52:38.172 --> 00:52:39.867
There you are.

892
00:52:41.143 --> 00:52:43.202
Oh, Cody. You're okay!

893
00:52:43.746 --> 00:52:44.940
- Oh...
- Oh-ho.

894
00:52:45.147 --> 00:52:46.273
What's with him?

895
00:52:46.513 --> 00:52:49.074
Enjoy it while it lasts.

896
00:52:49.517 --> 00:52:51.917
See, this is the kind of
white-knuckle adventure...

897
00:52:52.086 --> 00:52:54.578
...the power diva is all about.

898
00:52:54.757 --> 00:52:59.751
Imagine, me and like 11 of my besties
traveling the world and kicking butt.

899
00:53:00.396 --> 00:53:04.262
But also making time to hang out
by the pool and gossip.

900
00:53:04.431 --> 00:53:07.697
And at the end of every episode,
I'll slap somebody.

901
00:53:07.869 --> 00:53:10.201
It'll be a huge hit.

902
00:53:12.207 --> 00:53:15.267
Mm. Mm.

903
00:53:20.714 --> 00:53:22.579
Hey, guys.
We found some more firewood.

904
00:53:23.049 --> 00:53:24.711
Great. Have a seat.

905
00:53:24.919 --> 00:53:26.944
I saved you some dinner.

906
00:53:27.588 --> 00:53:30.456
- Uh...
- Oops. My bad.

907
00:53:31.725 --> 00:53:33.818
Was I not supposed to eat that?
Heh, heh, heh.

908
00:53:34.261 --> 00:53:36.560
Aagh! You knew that was for me, Tank.

909
00:53:36.764 --> 00:53:40.325
You snooze, you lose, bro.
Survival of the Tankiest.

910
00:53:40.501 --> 00:53:43.732
Came up with that myself.
I may change it to Hankiest later.

911
00:53:44.105 --> 00:53:47.561
Here, Cody.
I picked these fish heads out of the trash.

912
00:53:47.741 --> 00:53:50.676
I think there's still
some meat in this one.

913
00:53:50.844 --> 00:53:53.244
Nah, I got a better idea.

914
00:53:54.749 --> 00:53:57.013
Hey, what are you doing?

915
00:53:57.251 --> 00:53:58.912
Stop that! Hey, I mean it!

916
00:54:01.955 --> 00:54:03.286
You're dead.

917
00:54:04.024 --> 00:54:05.354
- Yeah.
- Whoa!

918
00:54:05.758 --> 00:54:07.852
- Uhn!
- Ls that all you got?

919
00:54:08.295 --> 00:54:11.128
Kick his butt.

920
00:54:11.631 --> 00:54:12.758
Heh, heh, heh.

921
00:54:13.734 --> 00:54:15.759
Whoa, whoa, wh...!

922
00:54:15.970 --> 00:54:19.166
Whoops! Sorry.
Just stretching my calf muscle.

923
00:54:19.739 --> 00:54:21.969
- Ha, ha! How do you like that?
- My tushy!

924
00:54:22.175 --> 00:54:24.974
Not cool, bro.
You can't trip my guy like that.

925
00:54:25.146 --> 00:54:27.011
Oh, yeah?
What do you wanna do about it?

926
00:54:27.181 --> 00:54:28.943
It's been a while, dude.

927
00:54:29.115 --> 00:54:32.641
- You think you can still handle it?
- Come on now, you can't see me.

928
00:54:32.818 --> 00:54:35.116
Yeah. I want a piece.

929
00:54:36.556 --> 00:54:39.286
Yeah! Take this.

930
00:54:39.459 --> 00:54:41.051
All right. Enough.

931
00:54:41.828 --> 00:54:44.457
It's supposed to be their fight,
remember?

932
00:54:46.565 --> 00:54:48.157
Yeah!

933
00:54:48.368 --> 00:54:52.030
One, two, three. That's it.
We have a winner.

934
00:54:52.204 --> 00:54:54.867
Ha! I kicked your butt with my butt.

935
00:54:55.075 --> 00:54:56.133
Oh, that smells.

936
00:54:56.309 --> 00:54:59.244
That was fun. Let me know
when you're ready for a rematch.

937
00:54:59.412 --> 00:55:02.175
I leave you alone for 10 minutes,
and this is what you do?

938
00:55:02.348 --> 00:55:04.339
I expect rookie mistakes from rookies...

939
00:55:04.517 --> 00:55:06.212
...but you guys know better.

940
00:55:06.385 --> 00:55:09.685
And, Cody Maverick,
we'll never get to the Trenches...

941
00:55:09.856 --> 00:55:12.256
...if you keep starting fights
with your teammates.

942
00:55:12.425 --> 00:55:14.791
Ah! Yeah. Ha, ha!

943
00:55:15.996 --> 00:55:19.556
Oh, wait.
Are we not doing this anymore?

944
00:55:19.732 --> 00:55:21.867
Oh, my bad.

945
00:55:22.201 --> 00:55:26.263
So other than getting
sat on, how do you think you're doing?

946
00:55:26.439 --> 00:55:29.499
Okay, that was not my fault, man.
Hunter called it too early.

947
00:55:29.676 --> 00:55:32.701
- I had Tank right where I wanted him.
- Ha-ha.

948
00:55:32.878 --> 00:55:34.004
Where, on your head?

949
00:55:34.179 --> 00:55:36.203
That's besides the point,
all right? Okay?

950
00:55:36.381 --> 00:55:39.545
Anyways, my head is still in the game,
if that's what you're asking.

951
00:55:39.718 --> 00:55:43.086
This is my one big chance to get off
Pen Gu and make something of myself.

952
00:55:43.256 --> 00:55:45.781
I'm gonna show the Hang 5
I've got what it takes.

953
00:55:45.959 --> 00:55:49.325
And I've been working out too.
Check this out. Can you tell?

954
00:55:50.029 --> 00:55:51.587
Uh! Oh...

955
00:55:51.897 --> 00:55:53.592
Oh, okay.

956
00:55:53.766 --> 00:55:56.395
Can you please go get J.C.?

957
00:56:02.373 --> 00:56:06.639
- Cock-a-doodle...
- You're gambling with your life, chicken.

958
00:56:10.849 --> 00:56:13.978
Right, yeah.

959
00:56:14.220 --> 00:56:15.915
Okay, got it.

960
00:56:16.089 --> 00:56:17.247
Good news, everyone.

961
00:56:17.455 --> 00:56:20.891
According to the conch,
we might reach the Trenches by nightfall.

962
00:56:21.092 --> 00:56:24.084
Then tomorrow morning, it's RTL.

963
00:56:24.262 --> 00:56:25.787
- RTL!
- RTL!

964
00:56:26.165 --> 00:56:28.565
Is anyone ever gonna tell us
what that means?

965
00:56:28.734 --> 00:56:31.498
What? And ruin the surprise?

966
00:56:31.671 --> 00:56:34.001
Hey, guys.
You might want to look at this.

967
00:56:34.572 --> 00:56:36.403
Anyone else get the feeling...

968
00:56:36.574 --> 00:56:40.067
...this island really doesn't want us
to reach the Trenches?

969
00:56:46.118 --> 00:56:48.243
Ideas, anybody?

970
00:56:49.519 --> 00:56:52.080
We sure didn't come this far
to give up now.

971
00:56:52.256 --> 00:56:54.247
The conch says
unless we can surf on fire...

972
00:56:54.425 --> 00:56:56.951
...we'll have to find
another way around.

973
00:56:57.129 --> 00:56:59.962
But this lava lake is huge.

974
00:57:01.133 --> 00:57:02.929
Come on, Cody.

975
00:57:05.203 --> 00:57:06.931
Surf...

976
00:57:07.972 --> 00:57:09.997
...on fire. Hey.

977
00:57:10.208 --> 00:57:11.436
Hey. Hey, guys, wait.

978
00:57:11.643 --> 00:57:13.270
When we were stuck in that tomb...

979
00:57:13.444 --> 00:57:16.505
...I saw some drawings
about a penguin who surfed through fire.

980
00:57:16.682 --> 00:57:19.672
I thought it was just a cool made-up story,
but what if it's not?

981
00:57:19.850 --> 00:57:21.819
What if somebody actually did it?

982
00:57:22.020 --> 00:57:25.512
I have an idea.
It's crazy, but I think it just might work.

983
00:57:25.723 --> 00:57:26.918
Spit it out, kid.

984
00:57:27.126 --> 00:57:29.457
Undertaker, quick, give me a boost.

985
00:57:34.297 --> 00:57:36.561
Who's up for some hang-gliding?

986
00:57:36.733 --> 00:57:39.362
- Yeah! That's awesome! Yeah!
- Let's go! Let's do it!

987
00:58:01.991 --> 00:58:05.826
Hey, Cody. Nice job coming up
with the idea for these hang gliders.

988
00:58:06.029 --> 00:58:10.330
This is the kind of creative, out-of-the-box
thinking we need in Hang 5.

989
00:58:10.535 --> 00:58:13.264
Ha, ha! Thanks, guys.
This is what I've been talking about.

990
00:58:13.470 --> 00:58:17.565
I've got all kinds of ideas.
Like dolphin-powered jet skis.

991
00:58:17.740 --> 00:58:20.004
Underwater breathing devices.
Hey, wait.

992
00:58:20.176 --> 00:58:25.843
What if we put wheels on our surfboards
so we can surf on dry land? Yeah?

993
00:58:26.049 --> 00:58:30.282
Whoa, wheels on a surfboard?
Let's not get too crazy here.

994
00:58:30.521 --> 00:58:32.680
Keep up the good work.

995
00:58:34.391 --> 00:58:37.450
Did you see that?
I'm gonna be in the Hang 5 for sure.

996
00:58:37.626 --> 00:58:39.356
So who's the loser now, huh?

997
00:58:39.529 --> 00:58:42.498
Whatever, chump. It ain't over yet.

998
00:58:42.699 --> 00:58:45.031
Oh, not according to
Mr. McMahon and Hunter.

999
00:58:45.203 --> 00:58:47.101
You better start
packing your bags, Tank.

1000
00:58:47.269 --> 00:58:49.760
Because tomorrow,
I'm gonna be part of the Hang 5.

1001
00:58:49.939 --> 00:58:52.738
Traveling the world,
doing the most radical stuff.

1002
00:58:52.909 --> 00:58:55.810
And you'll just go back to being
a nobody from nowhere island.

1003
00:58:56.012 --> 00:58:59.243
And you'll never see me again.

1004
00:58:59.416 --> 00:59:00.713
What?

1005
00:59:01.651 --> 00:59:03.743
You don't wanna go back to Pen Gu?

1006
00:59:03.919 --> 00:59:05.614
What about our surf school?

1007
00:59:05.788 --> 00:59:07.312
Lani, come on.

1008
00:59:07.523 --> 00:59:10.049
It's the Hang 5, okay?
I'm gonna be famous.

1009
00:59:10.227 --> 00:59:12.525
I'll be a hero to millions of kids.

1010
00:59:12.729 --> 00:59:15.927
But you're already a hero
to the kids back home.

1011
00:59:16.100 --> 00:59:17.793
And to me.

1012
00:59:18.033 --> 00:59:20.627
This is different. Can't you see that?

1013
00:59:20.803 --> 00:59:23.033
I'll be on the best surf team
on the planet.

1014
00:59:23.239 --> 00:59:26.333
I'll finally be somebody.
That's what really matters.

1015
00:59:26.542 --> 00:59:28.511
Hey, Cody. Check out my glider, dude.

1016
00:59:28.678 --> 00:59:29.667
Coming, J.C.

1017
00:59:29.846 --> 00:59:32.642
Come show me how this thing's
supposed to work. Ha-ha-ha.

1018
00:59:34.583 --> 00:59:36.847
Eh... Come on, Joe. Let's go.

1019
00:59:37.052 --> 00:59:41.490
I guess we're just a couple of nobodies
from nowhere island.

1020
00:59:50.799 --> 00:59:52.131
Let's be safe, guys.

1021
00:59:52.501 --> 00:59:53.866
This ain't the ocean.

1022
00:59:54.069 --> 00:59:57.835
If you wipe out up here,
you'll be a bucket of extra crispy.

1023
00:59:58.008 --> 01:00:02.306
Oh, man. Just like my uncle,
Chicken Fernando.

1024
01:00:02.944 --> 01:00:05.880
You're going down, twerp.
No more Mr. Nice Tank.

1025
01:00:06.080 --> 01:00:08.708
You are not gonna take my spot
on the Hang 5.

1026
01:00:08.883 --> 01:00:10.977
Okay, let's see what you got.

1027
01:00:11.220 --> 01:00:12.812
On your mark.

1028
01:00:17.358 --> 01:00:18.347
Get ready.

1029
01:00:19.494 --> 01:00:21.394
- Hey, watch it, man.
- Heh, heh, heh.

1030
01:00:21.596 --> 01:00:24.031
- Go!
- Yeah!

1031
01:00:24.800 --> 01:00:25.824
Oh.

1032
01:00:28.405 --> 01:00:30.338
Hot, hot, hot.

1033
01:00:32.107 --> 01:00:33.732
All right!

1034
01:00:50.425 --> 01:00:52.689
Loving the lava.

1035
01:01:09.277 --> 01:01:10.266
There you are.

1036
01:01:12.882 --> 01:01:14.508
You're gonna eat it, Tank.

1037
01:01:14.716 --> 01:01:17.741
- Show me what you got. You like that?
- That's not nice. Stop that.

1038
01:01:17.918 --> 01:01:20.250
- Hey, that's not fair. Whoa!
- This is fun.

1039
01:01:24.959 --> 01:01:27.018
Wait, I'm first?
Ha, ha, ha!

1040
01:01:27.195 --> 01:01:28.287
I'm first.

1041
01:01:28.463 --> 01:01:30.364
- Payback time. Ha, ha, ha!
- Oh!

1042
01:01:31.233 --> 01:01:34.792
Whoa! Whoa!

1043
01:01:34.968 --> 01:01:36.061
Whoa!

1044
01:01:36.303 --> 01:01:37.429
Grr...

1045
01:01:39.206 --> 01:01:41.607
Oh, you are not taking this
away from me, Tank.

1046
01:01:43.044 --> 01:01:44.671
- Got you.
- What are you doing?

1047
01:01:45.980 --> 01:01:47.243
Whoa! Whoa!

1048
01:01:47.447 --> 01:01:48.914
How do you like me now?

1049
01:01:49.082 --> 01:01:51.380
Oof! Aaah!

1050
01:01:51.585 --> 01:01:54.578
I don't want to be a combo meal!

1051
01:01:56.190 --> 01:01:58.590
Hang on, Joe! I got you, buddy.

1052
01:02:03.729 --> 01:02:07.598
Whoa. My board. No!

1053
01:02:15.576 --> 01:02:16.907
All right!

1054
01:02:17.511 --> 01:02:20.912
Who's awesome? I'm awesome.

1055
01:02:22.481 --> 01:02:23.676
What's going on, everyone?

1056
01:02:25.118 --> 01:02:28.087
The Undertaker saved me from death.

1057
01:02:28.255 --> 01:02:29.985
Ironic.

1058
01:02:30.658 --> 01:02:31.682
Where's your board?

1059
01:02:31.859 --> 01:02:34.621
You destroyed it
when you bumped Tank into Joe.

1060
01:02:34.794 --> 01:02:38.026
What? Joe, man, I'm so sorry.
I didn't mean to...

1061
01:02:38.198 --> 01:02:41.065
"Sorry" doesn't cut it, Cody.
What the heck were you thinking?

1062
01:02:41.234 --> 01:02:43.533
Yeah, man. What'd I ever do to you?

1063
01:02:43.738 --> 01:02:45.967
All these years of friendship.
And he still...

1064
01:02:47.474 --> 01:02:49.873
He still keeps these... These walls up.

1065
01:02:50.042 --> 01:02:53.273
And I don't know
how to break them down.

1066
01:02:54.648 --> 01:02:57.446
I just don't know what to think anymore.

1067
01:02:57.617 --> 01:02:59.016
Are you kidding me, dude?

1068
01:02:59.186 --> 01:03:01.883
This guy has been sabotaging me
since day one.

1069
01:03:02.056 --> 01:03:03.646
And you think that makes it okay?

1070
01:03:03.823 --> 01:03:05.814
Well, I... Yeah.

1071
01:03:05.992 --> 01:03:08.927
I was just trying to win.
So I could prove I can be one of you.

1072
01:03:09.095 --> 01:03:12.554
Putting your friends in danger
only proves that you're nothing like us.

1073
01:03:12.766 --> 01:03:14.461
The Hang 5 is a family.

1074
01:03:14.634 --> 01:03:18.399
We have each other's back,
no matter what.

1075
01:03:18.671 --> 01:03:22.038
Lani. Tell them I didn't mean for this
to happen. All right? You know me.

1076
01:03:22.541 --> 01:03:24.133
Yeah, Cody, I do.

1077
01:03:24.311 --> 01:03:27.906
And that's why
I'm just so disappointed in you right now.

1078
01:03:34.486 --> 01:03:36.978
And you were doing so well too.

1079
01:03:51.370 --> 01:03:53.929
I told you from the start
this kid's trouble.

1080
01:03:54.339 --> 01:03:55.932
He almost got the chicken killed.

1081
01:03:56.108 --> 01:03:57.700
That would have been on you, J.C.

1082
01:03:57.877 --> 01:03:59.742
Cody's not like that, Mr. McMahon.

1083
01:03:59.912 --> 01:04:02.177
He just got carried away
competing with Tank.

1084
01:04:02.349 --> 01:04:05.180
That guy's been acting like a jerk
this whole time.

1085
01:04:05.350 --> 01:04:07.581
I wanted to know
how Cody deals with problems...

1086
01:04:07.753 --> 01:04:09.414
...since you thought he was special.

1087
01:04:09.588 --> 01:04:11.613
And now I know. We're a team, J.C.

1088
01:04:12.124 --> 01:04:14.718
That kid doesn't care about
anything other than winning.

1089
01:04:14.894 --> 01:04:17.759
And he doesn't give two sand crabs
about who gets in his way.

1090
01:04:17.928 --> 01:04:20.363
Maybe that's what you saw in him
back at Pen Gu.

1091
01:04:20.532 --> 01:04:21.829
Have you thought about that?

1092
01:04:54.632 --> 01:04:56.567
Cock-a...

1093
01:04:56.735 --> 01:04:57.827
Oh, no.

1094
01:04:58.003 --> 01:04:59.560
You guys, come look at this.

1095
01:05:01.507 --> 01:05:06.067
"Joe, sorry for everything.
You deserve this more than me.

1096
01:05:06.243 --> 01:05:08.337
Your bro, Cody."

1097
01:05:08.513 --> 01:05:13.416
Ha, ha, ha! What a stupid note.
"You deserve this more than me."

1098
01:05:13.586 --> 01:05:16.680
Hey, is anybody else surprised
Chicken Joe can read? Ha, ha, ha!

1099
01:05:19.089 --> 01:05:21.683
We have to find Cody.
He couldn't have gotten that far.

1100
01:05:21.892 --> 01:05:24.486
That was pretty sad, bro.

1101
01:05:25.095 --> 01:05:26.393
Lani, wait.

1102
01:05:26.631 --> 01:05:30.499
I think you gotta let Cody
work things out on his own.

1103
01:05:30.935 --> 01:05:32.528
He'll come back when he's ready.

1104
01:05:32.705 --> 01:05:34.432
But how can you be sure?

1105
01:05:34.671 --> 01:05:36.468
I've been where he's at.

1106
01:05:36.640 --> 01:05:39.667
Trust me. He just needs time to think.

1107
01:05:43.916 --> 01:05:47.112
It's time we haul our butts
down to the Trenches.

1108
01:05:47.285 --> 01:05:49.683
The best waves come at dawn.

1109
01:05:49.852 --> 01:05:53.880
Does anyone else think
a storm is coming?

1110
01:05:54.057 --> 01:05:56.026
We're counting on it.

1111
01:05:56.194 --> 01:05:58.924
Oh, cool. Right on, then.

1112
01:06:15.547 --> 01:06:17.174
Whoa!

1113
01:06:23.086 --> 01:06:28.150
"Here lies the great hero
of Slaughter island...

1114
01:06:28.326 --> 01:06:32.318
...the bravest
and most honored surfer of all.

1115
01:06:37.600 --> 01:06:42.163
He gave up his chance
at fame and fortune...

1116
01:06:42.339 --> 01:06:45.707
...and he chose to stay with his people
to protect them...

1117
01:06:45.877 --> 01:06:48.435
...from the treacherous waters
of the Trenches...

1118
01:06:48.611 --> 01:06:54.607
...by performing the sacred rites
of Ride the Lightning."

1119
01:06:54.917 --> 01:06:55.906
RTL.

1120
01:06:57.721 --> 01:07:00.884
Oh, no. I gotta tell Lani and Joe.

1121
01:07:15.606 --> 01:07:17.096
Whoa!

1122
01:07:24.714 --> 01:07:27.411
My friends, we finally made it.

1123
01:07:27.584 --> 01:07:30.109
Behold, the Trenches.

1124
01:07:47.638 --> 01:07:50.469
Whoa. Look at all these
broken surfboards.

1125
01:07:50.639 --> 01:07:53.131
Must have been some major wipeouts.

1126
01:07:53.309 --> 01:07:56.904
I'm not gonna end up like them.
I'm way better than those guys.

1127
01:07:57.246 --> 01:08:01.444
Ladies and gentlemen,
the moment you've all been waiting for.

1128
01:08:08.490 --> 01:08:11.619
Hang 5, prepare to RTL!

1129
01:08:11.794 --> 01:08:14.058
RTL!

1130
01:08:14.997 --> 01:08:19.365
Wait a minute.
Are you telling me that RTL stands for...

1131
01:08:19.567 --> 01:08:22.161
Ride the Lightning.

1132
01:08:22.337 --> 01:08:26.103
Whoa! Wicked timing
on that delivery, bro.

1133
01:08:26.274 --> 01:08:29.836
Surfing during a lightning storm?
You actually planned for this?

1134
01:08:30.012 --> 01:08:32.503
Are you guys completely insane?

1135
01:08:32.682 --> 01:08:35.650
Well, yeah.
We figured you knew that about us.

1136
01:08:35.817 --> 01:08:39.150
Lani, we're all about pushing ourselves
to the absolute limit.

1137
01:08:39.321 --> 01:08:41.950
And it doesn't get any more extreme
than this.

1138
01:08:42.358 --> 01:08:45.383
I'm sorry, you guys. I can't do this.

1139
01:08:45.593 --> 01:08:48.686
Thank you for the opportunity,
but no, thank you.

1140
01:08:48.862 --> 01:08:50.193
This isn't for me.

1141
01:08:50.364 --> 01:08:53.163
Hey, we understand, love.
No hard feelings.

1142
01:08:53.501 --> 01:08:54.991
What about you, Chicken?

1143
01:08:55.403 --> 01:08:58.737
Are you ready
for a spot on the Hang 5?

1144
01:08:59.408 --> 01:09:02.502
I don't think I'm quite ready
for that big chicken bucket...

1145
01:09:02.678 --> 01:09:04.542
...up in the sky just yet.

1146
01:09:04.713 --> 01:09:09.046
Oh, hey.
How about an honorary membership?

1147
01:09:09.216 --> 01:09:11.549
Heh, heh, heh. You got it.

1148
01:09:16.759 --> 01:09:18.816
So how about it, Tank?

1149
01:09:18.992 --> 01:09:20.823
So, uh, all I gotta do...

1150
01:09:20.994 --> 01:09:24.487
- ...is surf one gigantic 50-foot wave.
- Yup.

1151
01:09:24.666 --> 01:09:27.191
It's in the middle of
a lightning-filled thunderstorm.

1152
01:09:27.369 --> 01:09:28.358
Oh, yeah.

1153
01:09:28.671 --> 01:09:31.605
Also off a beach
littered with jagged coral reef.

1154
01:09:31.773 --> 01:09:33.001
Exactly.

1155
01:09:33.208 --> 01:09:35.539
But then I'm in the Hang 5
and I'll be famous...

1156
01:09:35.709 --> 01:09:38.405
...and make lots of money
selling surf videos.

1157
01:09:38.645 --> 01:09:41.547
You gotta do more than surf it,
you gotta survive it.

1158
01:09:41.716 --> 01:09:43.547
And make it look good.

1159
01:09:44.786 --> 01:09:46.914
You in or you out?

1160
01:09:47.089 --> 01:09:49.851
Um... In?

1161
01:09:50.023 --> 01:09:53.049
In. I'm definitely in.
This is a good decision.

1162
01:09:53.360 --> 01:09:55.760
- Sweet. Headbutt for good luck.
- Oh!

1163
01:09:55.929 --> 01:09:58.591
Oh, yeah. I'm gonna miss that if I die.

1164
01:09:58.767 --> 01:10:00.029
Then let's RTL.

1165
01:10:00.201 --> 01:10:01.225
RTL!

1166
01:10:01.403 --> 01:10:03.303
Sweet! Yeah!

1167
01:10:04.737 --> 01:10:07.366
I can't watch. But I can't not watch.

1168
01:10:07.541 --> 01:10:09.099
I'm a lifeguard, Joe.

1169
01:10:09.276 --> 01:10:11.541
I'm supposed to protect
all beachgoers.

1170
01:10:11.713 --> 01:10:13.977
I swore a Hippocratic oath.

1171
01:10:14.182 --> 01:10:17.419
Hah. Hippos. They're rad.

1172
01:10:24.391 --> 01:10:26.723
Are you sure
we have to paddle out this far?

1173
01:10:26.894 --> 01:10:30.092
It seems far.
I can't even see the beach from here.

1174
01:10:30.265 --> 01:10:31.994
All right, here's how this works.

1175
01:10:32.200 --> 01:10:33.326
Don't panic.

1176
01:10:33.499 --> 01:10:36.560
Work as a team.
And keep an eye out for each other.

1177
01:10:36.737 --> 01:10:38.499
And we'll all make it through this.

1178
01:10:38.838 --> 01:10:40.305
Whoa!

1179
01:10:41.140 --> 01:10:43.837
Here we go, Tank.
This is your last test.

1180
01:10:44.011 --> 01:10:46.502
Mr. McMahon thinks
you're a yellow-bellied coward.

1181
01:10:46.713 --> 01:10:48.079
- But I told him...
- What?

1182
01:10:48.249 --> 01:10:50.772
...you were the real deal.
Don't let me down, Tank.

1183
01:10:50.950 --> 01:10:52.815
Or we'll all die.

1184
01:10:52.985 --> 01:10:57.116
Do not...
I repeat, do not go rogue out there.

1185
01:10:57.291 --> 01:10:59.225
We're all counting on each other.
Got it?

1186
01:11:00.661 --> 01:11:01.685
Okay, here it comes!

1187
01:11:01.862 --> 01:11:03.329
- Yes!
- All right!

1188
01:11:07.099 --> 01:11:09.499
Come on, Tank. It's go time.

1189
01:11:13.173 --> 01:11:15.038
Everybody, ready?

1190
01:11:15.242 --> 01:11:17.142
Yeah, I was born ready!

1191
01:11:17.311 --> 01:11:18.834
Oh, yeah!

1192
01:11:22.248 --> 01:11:23.236
Whoa!

1193
01:11:29.522 --> 01:11:31.354
- Ha-ha-ha.
- Come on.

1194
01:11:37.396 --> 01:11:40.058
This is the moment
we've been waiting for!

1195
01:11:40.266 --> 01:11:42.701
Whoa, this is amazing!

1196
01:11:44.371 --> 01:11:45.359
Let's ride!

1197
01:11:45.538 --> 01:11:47.130
Yeah!

1198
01:11:54.380 --> 01:11:56.314
- No way, man. No, I can't do it.
- Whoa!

1199
01:11:56.816 --> 01:11:58.511
Tank, don't!

1200
01:12:02.289 --> 01:12:05.017
Stay in formation. It's the only way.

1201
01:12:14.734 --> 01:12:16.326
Don't let it touch you.

1202
01:12:16.502 --> 01:12:17.662
Unh!

1203
01:12:17.904 --> 01:12:19.928
Undertaker, I'm coming for you.

1204
01:12:20.539 --> 01:12:22.439
- Look out!
- We're not gonna make it!

1205
01:12:33.619 --> 01:12:37.452
Help! I got him, he's been hit.

1206
01:12:39.524 --> 01:12:42.322
Move aside! I can save him.

1207
01:12:45.431 --> 01:12:46.830
Oh, I hope I'm not too late.

1208
01:12:56.942 --> 01:12:59.069
Whoa! Good to get out of that mess.

1209
01:13:00.445 --> 01:13:01.435
Oh, crap.

1210
01:13:03.847 --> 01:13:05.246
No!

1211
01:13:08.453 --> 01:13:10.887
Ah. Ooh!

1212
01:13:11.856 --> 01:13:13.620
No!

1213
01:13:15.093 --> 01:13:18.290
Oh, man.
This thing is like a lightning rod.

1214
01:13:18.463 --> 01:13:19.895
No!

1215
01:13:22.666 --> 01:13:23.997
Help!

1216
01:13:27.772 --> 01:13:29.501
Tank! Hang on, I'm coming.

1217
01:13:37.748 --> 01:13:39.511
Hunter!

1218
01:13:40.250 --> 01:13:43.242
Hunter, Hanky needs you.

1219
